desc:CZ77 (v2) [synth] (GFX)
//tags: instrument synth phase distortion digital bells strings pads leads
//author: GardenFX
// by JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
// Requires gfx-drift, gfx-output, gfx-thick, gfx-clip (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// CZ77 - a phase distortion synthesiser, in the spirit of the mid-1980s phase distortion digital synthesisers known
// for glass-like metallic bells, expressive plucked strings, evolving pads and aggressive cutting leads. Every sound
// is synthesised.
//
// SIGNAL FLOW
//   Two LINES per voice (8 voices). Each line: a DCO (a cosine read through a bent phase - PHASE DISTORTION) -> DCW
//   (how far the phase is bent: 0 = a pure sine, up to the full wave) -> DCA (its level). The DCO, DCW and DCA each
//   have an 8-step ENVELOPE (a RATE and a LEVEL per step, a SUSTAIN step and an END step).
//   WAVES (8): SAW, SQUARE, PULSE, DOUBLE (double sine), SAW-PULSE, RESO I, RESO II, RESO III (a resonant peak
//   that sweeps up the harmonics with the DCW, in a saw, triangle or trapezoid window). Each line plays a first wave
//   and, if one is chosen, a second: the two alternate cycle by cycle.
//   LINE SELECT: LINE 1, LINE 2, 1 + 2 (both, line 2 detuned by DETUNE), 1 + 1' (line 1 doubled, the copy detuned).
//   RING: line 2 ring-modulated by line 1. NOISE: line 2's pitch scrambled by noise (breath, wind, FX).
//   DCW KEY FOLLOW: the higher the key, the less the DCW (brightness evens out up the keyboard). DCA KEY FOLLOW: the
//   higher the key, the faster its envelope. DCW DEPTH scales both lines' DCW envelopes; VELOCITY reaches level and DCW.
//   -> FILTER (OFF by default; LP / BP / HP, CUTOFF, RESO, KEY TRACK, ENV from line 1's DCW envelope) -> VIBRATO
//   (TRIANGLE / SAW UP / SAW DOWN / SQUARE, DELAY, RATE, DEPTH; DCW MOD: the same LFO, faded in over the same DELAY,
//   breathes both lines' DCW - a slow formant shimmer) -> the 8 voices (or one in MONO: legato - a key played while
//   another is held slides there over GLIDE without restarting the envelopes; letting go slides back to the newest
//   key still held) -> FX strip -> THICK -> house output stage
//   (CLIP, ceiling -0.3 dBFS) -> LEVEL.
//   FX STRIP (each with its title lamp, crossfaded in and out): PHASER (6 stages: RATE, DEPTH, FEEDBACK; left and right a
//   quarter-cycle apart) -> CHORUS (the original's stereo BBD chorus: three delay lines swept by a three-phase LFO, a
//   slow 0.56 Hz sweep and a fast 7.14 Hz shimmer mixed 10:1; RATE scales both, DEPTH, MIX) -> DRIVE (AMOUNT into the
//   house anti-aliased soft clipper, level-matched; TONE) -> COMP (THRESHOLD, RATIO, ATTACK, RELEASE, automatic make-up,
//   stereo-linked) -> DELAY (ping-pong: TIME a note value with SYNC lit, or ms; FEEDBACK, DAMPING in the loop, MIX).
//   The oscillators run at twice the sample rate (a half-band filter brings them down): the sharp phase bends stay
//   clean up the keyboard. Latency: 16 samples (reported).
// DRIFT (0 - 100 %, 50 % = standard): oscillator phase jitter, each voice's pitch wandering (+/-20 cents slow, +/-6
//   cents a note), the wave tables' rounding wandering (about 13 bits at 50 %, 12 at 100 %), and a slow thermal drift
//   in the output (level +/-0.25 dB, a touch of warmth).
// GUI: LINES (blue keys: LINE 1, LINE 2, 1 + 2, 1 + 1'; RING, NOISE, MONO; DETUNE: OCTAVE, NOTE, FINE; GLIDE), WAVES (the LINE 1 /
//   LINE 2 tabs choose the line being edited; pastel keys (a shade per wave) with their own red LEDs: the WAVE, then the SECOND WAVE - click
//   it again to turn it off; DCW DEPTH, DCW / DCA FOLLOW, LINE 2 LEVEL, VELOCITY), ENVELOPES (DCO / DCW / DCA tabs; the
//   display: drag a point up / down for its level, left / right for its rate - Shift fine; the wheel sets the level,
//   Shift + wheel the rate; a light dot rides the newest note; STEP arrows, RATE and LEVEL readouts, SUSTAIN and END
//   menus), FILTER, VIBRATO (with DCW MOD), the FX strip, OUTPUT (LEVEL, DRIFT, IN with its amber LED and the pilot lamp, THICK, the
//   OUT meter); 8 voice lamps in the top bar; S / M / L / ?. The keys follow the original's flat blue / grey / black caps.
// MIDI: 8 voices (two lines each) or MONO (legato, a held-note stack), click-free stealing (a 3 ms fade), pitch bend +/-2 st, mod wheel (vibrato), sustain
//   pedal, all-notes-off (CC 120 / 123), released when the transport stops; MIDI passes through. A change of wave, line
//   or RING / NOISE dips the voices for 6 ms; every FX setting glides - presets change without a click.
// PRESETS (level-matched: held about -23 dBFS RMS, the struck ones peaking about -8 dBFS): Default, Glass Bell (ring-
//   modulated, a long decay), Phase Strings (1 + 1', slow DCW, chorus), Electric Piano (sine + a pulse tine an octave
//   up), Brass Lead (DCW swell, a fall into the note, drive), Resonant Sweep (RESO I swept up and down, delay), Ambient
//   Pad (DOUBLE alternating with RESO II, 1 + 1', phaser, chorus, delay), Metallic Pluck (ring, short), Dirty Sync Bass
//   (RESO III with a square an octave down, drive, comp), Chorus Organ (8' + 4' squares, the chorus), Sci-Fi FX (noise
//   modulation, pitch sweeps, ping-pong delay), Soft Evolution (a DCW that rises, falls and rises again),
//   Synth Bass, Breathy Flute (noise breath), Funky Clav, Vibes, Reso Lead, Sync Lead, Digital Choir, Tubular Bells, Marimba,
//   Harpsichord, Reso Bass, Night Wind (noise, a DCW that breathes), and three in the spirit of the 70s modular orchestral
//   albums: Space Choir (saw + pulse, a slow multi-step formant swell, DCW MOD), Synth Strings (a saw with a resonant
//   line an octave up that fades faster, more DRIFT) and Space Flute (MONO with GLIDE, a breath chiff, delayed vibrato).
// STATUS: v1.1 - in the Lab (Oct 2026): 27 presets, MONO / GLIDE, DCW MOD.

import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-thick.jsfx-inc
import gfx-clip.jsfx-inc

out_pin:left output
out_pin:right output

slider1:line_md=0<0,3,1{Line 1,Line 2,Line 1 + 2,Line 1 + 1'}>-Line select
slider2:ring=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Ring modulation
slider3:noise=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Noise modulation
slider4:l1_w1=0<0,7,1{Saw,Square,Pulse,Double sine,Saw-pulse,Reso I,Reso II,Reso III}>-Line 1 wave
slider5:l1_w2=0<0,8,1{Off,Saw,Square,Pulse,Double sine,Saw-pulse,Reso I,Reso II,Reso III}>-Line 1 second wave
slider6:l2_w1=0<0,7,1{Saw,Square,Pulse,Double sine,Saw-pulse,Reso I,Reso II,Reso III}>-Line 2 wave
slider7:l2_w2=0<0,8,1{Off,Saw,Square,Pulse,Double sine,Saw-pulse,Reso I,Reso II,Reso III}>-Line 2 second wave
slider8:det_oct=0<-2,2,1>-Detune octave
slider9:det_note=0<0,11,1>-Detune note
slider10:det_fine=0<0,60,1>-Detune fine (cents)
slider11:l1_dkf=30<0,100,1>-Line 1 DCW key follow (%)
slider12:l1_akf=30<0,100,1>-Line 1 DCA key follow (%)
slider13:l2_dkf=30<0,100,1>-Line 2 DCW key follow (%)
slider14:l2_akf=30<0,100,1>-Line 2 DCA key follow (%)
slider15:dcw_dep=100<0,100,1>-DCW depth (%)
slider16:l2_lvl=0<-24,6,0.1>-Line 2 level (dB)
slider17:flt_md=0<0,3,1{Off,LP,BP,HP}>-Filter mode
slider18:flt_cut=8000<40,20000,1:log>-Filter cutoff (Hz)
slider19:flt_res=0<0,100,1>-Filter resonance (%)
slider20:flt_kt=0<0,100,1>-Filter key track (%)
slider21:flt_env=0<-100,100,1>-Filter env (%)
slider22:vsens=50<0,100,1>-Velocity (%)
slider23:vib_wv=0<0,3,1{Triangle,Saw up,Saw down,Square}>-Vibrato wave
slider24:vib_dly=0.3<0,3,0.01>-Vibrato delay (s)
slider25:vib_rate=5<0.1,12,0.01:log>-Vibrato rate (Hz)
slider26:vib_dep=0<0,100,1>-Vibrato depth (cents)
slider27:vol=0<-18,6,0.1>-Output level (dB)
slider28:drift=50<0,100,1>-Drift (%)
slider29:in_on=1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-In
slider30:thick=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Thick
slider31:ph_on=0<0,1,1{Out,In}>-Phaser
slider32:ph_rate=0.4<0.05,8,0.01:log>-Phaser rate (Hz)
slider33:ph_dep=60<0,100,1>-Phaser depth (%)
slider34:ph_fb=40<0,90,1>-Phaser feedback (%)
slider35:ch_on=0<0,1,1{Out,In}>-Chorus
slider36:ch_rate=1<0.25,4,0.01:log>-Chorus rate (x)
slider37:ch_dep=60<0,100,1>-Chorus depth (%)
slider38:ch_mix=50<0,100,1>-Chorus mix (%)
slider39:dr_on=0<0,1,1{Out,In}>-Drive
slider40:dr_amt=30<0,100,1>-Drive amount (%)
slider41:dr_tone=60<0,100,1>-Drive tone (%)
slider42:cp_on=0<0,1,1{Out,In}>-Comp
slider43:cp_thr=-18<-40,0,0.1>-Comp threshold (dB)
slider44:cp_rat=4<1,20,0.1:log>-Comp ratio
slider45:cp_att=10<0.1,100,0.1:log>-Comp attack (ms)
slider46:cp_rel=150<10,1000,1:log>-Comp release (ms)
slider47:dl_on=0<0,1,1{Out,In}>-Delay
slider48:dl_sync=1<0,1,1{Free,Sync}>-Delay time mode
slider49:dl_div=7<0,12,1{1/32,1/16 T,1/16,1/8 T,1/16 D,1/8,1/4 T,1/8 D,1/4,1/2 T,1/4 D,1/2,1 bar}>-Delay time (sync)
slider50:dl_ms=375<10,2000,1:log>-Delay time (ms)
slider51:dl_fb=35<0,95,1>-Delay feedback (%)
slider52:dl_damp=5000<1000,18000,1:log>-Delay damping (Hz)
slider53:dl_mix=25<0,100,1>-Delay mix (%)
slider54:mono=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Mono (legato)
slider55:glide=80<1,2000,1:log>-Glide (ms)
slider56:dcw_mod=0<0,100,1>-DCW mod (%)
slider57:prs_sel=0<0,27,1{No preset,Default,Glass Bell,Phase Strings,Electric Piano,Brass Lead,Resonant Sweep,Ambient Pad,Metallic Pluck,Dirty Sync Bass,Chorus Organ,Sci-Fi FX,Soft Evolution,Synth Bass,Breathy Flute,Funky Clav,Vibes,Reso Lead,Sync Lead,Digital Choir,Tubular Bells,Marimba,Harpsichord,Reso Bass,Night Wind,Space Choir,Synth Strings,Space Flute}>-Preset

@init
#ui_man = "gfx-g-cz77-v2";
ext_noinit = 1;
!ui_dflt ? ( ui_sz = 0;  pr_cur = 1; );
ui_dflt = 1;
CR = 16;

// ---------- memory map ----------
NV = 8;  VS = 128;  VOX = 30000;         // voice records
MQ = 4096;  MQMAX = 1000;                // the MIDI queue
MSTK = 1200;                             // MONO: the held-note stack (up to 64 notes)
E = 40000;  ES = 20;                     // the envelopes: E + (line * 3 + env) * ES: [0..7] rates, [8..15] levels, [16] sustain step (-1 off), [17] end step
HB = 41000;  HBN = 64;                   // the half-band (2x -> 1x): coefficients, then the history (2 x 64)
VD = 1000;                               // voice lamps (audio -> GUI): DCA level per voice
CHB = 1500000;  CHN = 8192;              // the chorus line (mono in, three taps)
DLB = 2000000;  DLN = 524288;            // the delay lines (L, R): up to 2.7 s at 192 kHz

// voice record fields
F_ON = 0;  F_NOTE = 1;  F_VEL = 2;  F_AGE = 3;  F_GATE = 4;  F_SUS = 5;  F_FADE = 6;  F_STEAL = 7;  F_PEND = 8;  F_PVEL = 9;
F_P1 = 10;  F_P2 = 11;  F_C1 = 12;  F_C2 = 13;  F_I1 = 14;  F_I2 = 15;      // phases, cycle parity, increments (at 2x)
F_EN = 16;                               // envelopes: F_EN + (line * 3 + env) * 4: value, step, state (0 run, 1 held at sustain, 2 done)
F_W1 = 40;  F_WS1 = 41;  F_A1 = 42;  F_AS1 = 43;     // line 1: DCW now + per-sample step, DCA now + step
F_W2 = 44;  F_WS2 = 45;  F_A2 = 46;  F_AS2 = 47;     // line 2
F_FS1 = 48;  F_FS2 = 49;  F_FG = 50;  F_FK = 51;     // the filter: states, coefficient, damping
F_DV = 52;  F_DT = 53;  F_DTM = 54;  F_NDT = 55;     // DRIFT: pitch wander value, target, timer; per-note offset
F_VT = 56;  F_GAIN = 57;  F_DVEL = 58;  F_LIVE = 59;  // time since the note began (vibrato delay), velocity gains, a line still sounding
F_NZ = 60;                               // noise modulation state
F_GL = 61;                               // MONO: the gliding pitch (note number)

memset(VOX, 0, NV * VS);  memset(VD, 0, 16);  memset(CHB, 0, CHN);  memset(DLB, 0, 2 * DLN);
ch_w = 0;  dl_w = 0;  ph_p = 0;  ch_pa = 0;  ch_pb = 0;

// ---------- the envelopes: a first-load default (presets set their own) ----------
function env_set(l, k, r0, l0, r1, l1, r2, l2, r3, l3, sus, en) local(b) (
  b = E + (l * 3 + k) * ES;  memset(b, 0, ES);
  b[0] = r0;  b[8] = l0;  b[1] = r1;  b[9] = l1;  b[2] = r2;  b[10] = l2;  b[3] = r3;  b[11] = l3;
  k = 4;  loop(4, b[k] = 50;  b[8 + k] = 0;  k += 1; );
  b[16] = sus;  b[17] = en;
);
function env_default() local(l) (
  l = 0;
  loop(2,
    env_set(l, 0, 99, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 0);                // DCO: flat
    env_set(l, 1, 85, 75, 55, 35, 45, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);               // DCW: a bright start settling, closing on release
    env_set(l, 2, 99, 99, 70, 80, 60, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);               // DCA: up, a little down, sustain, release
    l += 1; );
);
!env_ok ? ( env_default();  env_ok = 1; );

// ---------- the half-band (63 taps, Kaiser): 2x -> 1x ----------
function hb_build() local(i, n, x, w, s, bes, t, k, sum) (
  n = 63;  sum = 0;  i = 0;
  loop(n,
    x = i - 31;
    s = x == 0 ? 0.5 : sin($pi * x * 0.5) / ($pi * x);
    t = x / 31;  t = 8 * sqrt(max(0, 1 - t * t));                     // Kaiser, beta 8 (I0 by its series)
    w = 1;  bes = 1;  k = 1;  loop(20, bes *= (t * 0.5 / k) * (t * 0.5 / k);  w += bes;  k += 1; );
    HB[i] = s * w;  sum += HB[i];  i += 1; );
  i = 0;  loop(n, HB[i] /= sum;  i += 1; );
  memset(HB + 64, 0, 128);  hb_w = 0;
);
hb_build();

pdc_bot_ch = 0;  pdc_top_ch = 2;  pdc_delay = 16;

ost_init(0);  ostL.ost_ch_init();  ostR.ost_ch_init();
thk_init();
dr_p.drift_init(0.6 + rand(1) * 0.4);  dr_q.drift_init(0.3 + rand(1) * 0.3);  dr_t.drift_init(0.2 + rand(1) * 0.2);
bend = 0;  sustain = 0;  age_n = 0;  cr_n = 0;  vib_ph = 0;  dc_r = 1 - 2 * $pi * 5 / srate;
in_x = in_on >= 0.5;  thk_x = 0;

// ---------- helpers ----------
function frac3(x) ( x - floor(x); );
function ts(x) ( x = max(-3, min(3, x));  x * (27 + x * x) / (27 + 9 * x * x); );
// a step's time to cross the full range (rate 99 = 1.5 ms, rate 0 = about 4 s)
function rtime(r) ( 0.0015 * 2 ^ ((99 - r) / 8.7); );

// ---------- PHASE DISTORTION: the 8 waves (p = phase 0..1, d = DCW 0..1, m = the sharpest bend the sample rate allows) ----------
function pdw(w, p, d, m) local(x, y, q, t, h, k, win) (
  w == 0 ? (                                                             // SAW: the phase rushes through the first half
    x = max(0.5 - 0.5 * d, m);  q = p < x ? 0.5 * p / x : 0.5 + 0.5 * (p - x) / (1 - x);  cos(2 * $pi * q);
  ) : w == 1 ? (                                                         // SQUARE: each half rushes, then holds
    h = p >= 0.5;  t = 2 * p - h;  x = max(1 - d, 2 * m);  q = 0.5 * h + 0.5 * min(t / x, 1);  cos(2 * $pi * q);
  ) : w == 2 ? (                                                         // PULSE: one quick cycle, then rest
    x = max(1 - d, m);  q = min(p / x, 1);  cos(2 * $pi * q);
  ) : w == 3 ? (                                                         // DOUBLE SINE: the first half speeds up, the second slows
    q = p < 0.5 ? p * (1 + d) : 0.5 * (1 + d) + (p - 0.5) * (1 - d);  cos(2 * $pi * q);
  ) : w == 4 ? (                                                         // SAW-PULSE: a saw in the first half, a rest in the second
    x = max(0.5 - 0.5 * d, m);  y = max(1 - x - 0.5 * d, m);
    q = p < x ? 0.5 * p / x : p < x + y ? 0.5 + 0.5 * (p - x) / y : 1;  cos(2 * $pi * q);
  ) : (                                                                  // RESO I / II / III: a resonant peak in a window
    k = min(1 + d * 14, 0.45 / max(m, 0.000001));
    win = w == 5 ? 1 - p : w == 6 ? ( p < 0.5 ? 2 * p : 2 - 2 * p ) : ( p < 0.5 ? 1 : 2 - 2 * p );
    (cos(2 * $pi * k * p) - 1) * win + (w == 7 ? 0.75 : 0.5);
  );
);

// ---------- the envelopes: one tick (o = the field, eb = its data, sp = full range per tick) ----------
function env_tk(b, o, eb, spd) local(v, i, st, lv, df, en, su) (
  v = b[o];  i = b[o + 1];  st = b[o + 2];
  st == 3 ? ( v = max(0, v - spd / rtime(eb[eb[17]]));  v <= 0 ? st = 2; ) :
  st != 2 && !(st == 1 && (b[F_GATE] || b[F_SUS])) ? (
    st = 0;
    lv = eb[8 + i] / 99;  df = lv - v;
    abs(df) <= spd / rtime(eb[i]) ? (
      v = lv;  en = eb[17];  su = eb[16];
      i >= en ? st = 2 : (i == su && (b[F_GATE] || b[F_SUS])) ? st = 1 : i += 1;
    ) : v += sign(df) * spd / rtime(eb[i]);
  );
  b[o] = v;  b[o + 1] = i;  b[o + 2] = st;
  v;
);
function env_line(k) ( floor(k / 3) == 1 && lmd == 3 ? 0 : floor(k / 3); );   // in 1 + 1' line 2 follows line 1's envelopes
// the key is let go: every envelope jumps to the step after its sustain step (if it hasn't passed it)
function env_rel(b) local(k, o, eb, su) (
  k = 0;
  loop(6, o = b + F_EN + k * 4;  eb = E + (env_line(k) * 3 + k % 3) * ES;  su = eb[16];
    su >= 0 && o[1] <= su ? ( su < eb[17] ? ( o[1] = su + 1;  o[2] = 0; ) : o[2] = 2; ) : o[2] == 1 ? o[2] = 0;
    k % 3 == 2 && (su < 0 || su >= eb[17]) ? o[2] = 3;                   // a DCA with nothing after its sustain (or none): it dies away
    k += 1; );
);

// ---------- one voice's control tick: envelopes, pitch, DCW, DCA, filter ----------
function v_tick(b) local(l, sp, kp, pe, dw, da, kf, st, f, t, inc, a, vb_, eb, w_t, a_t, vf, dmv) (
  kp = max(0, min(1, (b[F_NOTE] - 36) / 60));                          // KEY FOLLOW: 0 at C2, 1 at C7
  b[F_VT] += CR / srate;
  // DRIFT: each voice's pitch wanders (a new target every 1.5 - 4 s)
  b[F_DTM] -= CR / srate * dm_s;  b[F_DTM] <= 0 ? ( b[F_DT] = rand(2) - 1;  b[F_DTM] = 1.5 + rand(1) * 2.5; );
  b[F_DV] += (b[F_DT] - b[F_DV]) * dr_c;
  vf = max(0, min(1, (b[F_VT] - 0.5 * vib_dly) / (0.5 * vib_dly + 0.001)));
  vb_ = vib_v * (vib_d * vf + modw * 30);                               // VIBRATO (cents): it fades in over its DELAY; the mod wheel adds
  b[F_GL] += (b[F_NOTE] - b[F_GL]) * gl_c;                              // GLIDE (MONO): the pitch slides to the note
  dmv = 1 + dcw_m * vf * vib_v;                                         // DCW MOD: the same LFO (and delay) breathes the DCW
  b[F_LIVE] = 0;
  l = 0;
  loop(2,
    (l == 0 && lmd != 1) || (l == 1 && lmd != 0) ? (
      sp = CR / srate * (1 + akf[l] * 3 * kp);                         // DCA KEY FOLLOW speeds every envelope up the keyboard
      eb = E + (env_line(l * 3) * 3) * ES;
      pe = env_tk(b, F_EN + (l * 3) * 4, eb, CR / srate);              // DCO: up to +24 semitones
      dw = env_tk(b, F_EN + (l * 3 + 1) * 4, eb + ES, CR / srate);
      da = env_tk(b, F_EN + (l * 3 + 2) * 4, eb + 2 * ES, sp);
      // pitch
      f = b[F_GL] + bend + pe * 24 + b[F_NDT] + b[F_DV] * 0.2 * dm_a + vb_ * 0.01 + (l == 1 && lmd >= 2 ? det_st : 0);
      inc = min(0.24, 440 * 2 ^ ((f - 69) / 12) / (2 * srate));        // per 2x sample
      l == 0 ? b[F_I1] = inc : b[F_I2] = inc;
      // DCW and DCA: ramp to the new values over the tick
      kf = 1 - dkf[l] * 0.85 * kp;
      w_t = max(0, min(0.995, dw * dcw_d * kf * b[F_DVEL] * dmv));
      a_t = (2 ^ (8 * da) - 1) / 255 * b[F_GAIN] * (l == 1 ? l2_g : 1) * (lmd >= 2 ? 0.7 : 1);   // two lines: each a little lower
      l == 0 ? ( b[F_WS1] = (w_t - b[F_W1]) / (2 * CR);  b[F_AS1] = (a_t - b[F_A1]) / (2 * CR); )
             : ( b[F_WS2] = (w_t - b[F_W2]) / (2 * CR);  b[F_AS2] = (a_t - b[F_A2]) / (2 * CR); );
      st = b[F_EN + (l * 3 + 2) * 4 + 2];
      !(st == 2 && da < 0.002 && !b[F_GATE] && !b[F_SUS]) || a_t > 0.00005 ? b[F_LIVE] = 1;
      l == 0 ? ( f_dw = dw; );
    ) : ( l == 0 ? ( b[F_AS1] = -b[F_A1] / (2 * CR);  b[F_WS1] = 0; ) : ( b[F_AS2] = -b[F_A2] / (2 * CR);  b[F_WS2] = 0; ); );
    l += 1;
  );
  // FILTER: cut-off with KEY TRACK and ENV (line 1's DCW envelope)
  fmd ? (
    f = max(20, min(fcut * 2 ^ (fkt * (b[F_NOTE] - 60) / 12 + fenv * 6 * f_dw), 0.24 * 2 * srate));
    t = tan($pi * f / (2 * srate));  b[F_FG] = t;  b[F_FK] = fk;
  );
  !b[F_LIVE] && !b[F_STEAL] ? b[F_ON] = 0;
);

// ---------- voices ----------
function v_start(b, note, vel) local(k) (
  b[F_ON] = 1;  b[F_NOTE] = note;  b[F_VEL] = vel;  b[F_GATE] = 1;  b[F_SUS] = 0;  age_n += 1;  b[F_AGE] = age_n;
  b[F_FADE] = 1;  b[F_STEAL] = 0;  b[F_VT] = 0;  b[F_LIVE] = 1;
  b[F_GAIN] = 1 - vsn + vsn * vel / 127;  b[F_DVEL] = 1 - 0.5 * vsn + 0.5 * vsn * vel / 127;
  k = 0;  loop(6, b[F_EN + k * 4 + 1] = 0;  b[F_EN + k * 4 + 2] = 0;  k += 1; );         // every envelope from step 1 (levels carry on)
  b[F_A1] < 0.0001 && b[F_A2] < 0.0001 ? (
    b[F_P1] = 0;  b[F_P2] = 0;  b[F_C1] = 0;  b[F_C2] = 0;  b[F_FS1] = 0;  b[F_FS2] = 0;
    k = 0;  loop(6, b[F_EN + k * 4] = 0;  k += 1; );
    b[F_DV] = rand(2) - 1;  b[F_DT] = rand(2) - 1;  b[F_DTM] = rand(1) * 2;
    b[F_P2] = lmd == 3 ? rand(1) * 0.25 : 0;
  );
  b[F_NDT] = (rand(2) - 1) * 0.06 * dm_a;                              // DRIFT: +/-6 cents a note at 50 %
  b[F_GL] = note;
  v_tick(b);
);
function v_alloc(note, vel) local(v, b, best, bq, q) (
  best = 0;  bq = 1000000000;  v = 0;
  loop(NV, b = VOX + v * VS;
    q = !b[F_ON] ? -1 : (!b[F_GATE] && !b[F_SUS]) ? b[F_A1] + b[F_A2] : 2 + b[F_AGE];
    b[F_ON] && b[F_NOTE] == note && !b[F_STEAL] ? q = -2;
    q < bq ? ( bq = q;  best = v; );  v += 1; );
  b = VOX + best * VS;
  b[F_ON] && (b[F_A1] + b[F_A2]) > 0.0005 && b[F_NOTE] != note ? ( b[F_STEAL] = 1;  b[F_PEND] = note;  b[F_PVEL] = vel; ) : v_start(b, note, vel);
);
function v_release(note) local(v, b) (
  v = 0;
  loop(NV, b = VOX + v * VS;
    b[F_ON] && b[F_GATE] && b[F_NOTE] == note ? ( b[F_GATE] = 0;  sustain ? b[F_SUS] = 1 : env_rel(b); );
    b[F_STEAL] && b[F_PEND] == note ? b[F_PEND] = -1;
    v += 1; );
);
function v_pedal_up() local(v, b) ( v = 0;  loop(NV, b = VOX + v * VS;  b[F_SUS] ? ( b[F_SUS] = 0;  env_rel(b); );  v += 1; ); );
function v_all_off() local(v, b) ( ms_n = 0;  v = 0;  loop(NV, b = VOX + v * VS;  b[F_ON] && (b[F_GATE] || b[F_SUS]) ? ( b[F_GATE] = 0;  b[F_SUS] = 0;  env_rel(b); );  v += 1; ); );
// MONO (legato): one voice; a key played while another is held glides there (GLIDE) without restarting the envelopes;
// letting go returns to the newest key still held
function mo_on(note, vel) local(b, k, j) (
  b = VOX;  k = 0;  j = 0;
  loop(ms_n, MSTK[k] != note ? ( MSTK[j] = MSTK[k];  j += 1; );  k += 1; );  ms_n = min(j, 63);  MSTK[ms_n] = note;  ms_n += 1;
  ms_n > 1 && b[F_ON] && b[F_GATE] ? ( b[F_NOTE] = note;  gl_c >= 1 ? b[F_GL] = note; ) : v_start(b, note, vel);
);
function mo_off(note) local(b, k, j) (
  b = VOX;  k = 0;  j = 0;
  loop(ms_n, MSTK[k] != note ? ( MSTK[j] = MSTK[k];  j += 1; );  k += 1; );  ms_n = j;
  b[F_ON] && b[F_GATE] && b[F_NOTE] == note ? (
    ms_n > 0 ? ( b[F_NOTE] = MSTK[ms_n - 1];  gl_c >= 1 ? b[F_GL] = b[F_NOTE]; ) : ( b[F_GATE] = 0;  sustain ? b[F_SUS] = 1 : env_rel(b); );
  );
);
function midi_event(i) local(st, d1, d2, c) (
  st = MQ[i * 4 + 1] & 0xF0;  d1 = MQ[i * 4 + 2];  d2 = MQ[i * 4 + 3];
  st == 0x90 && d2 > 0 ? ( mo_m ? mo_on(d1, d2) : v_alloc(d1, d2); ) :
  (st == 0x80 || (st == 0x90 && d2 == 0)) ? ( mo_m ? mo_off(d1) : v_release(d1); ) :
  st == 0xE0 ? bend = ((d2 * 128 + d1) - 8192) / 8192 * 2 :
  st == 0xB0 ? (
    d1 == 1 ? modw = d2 / 127 :
    d1 == 64 ? ( c = d2 >= 64;  sustain && !c ? v_pedal_up();  sustain = c; ) :
    (d1 == 123 || d1 == 120) ? v_all_off();
  );
);

// ---------- one voice, one 2x sample ----------
function v_run(b) local(p, d, m, y, y1, y2, w, ws, g, v1, v2, v3, a1, nz) (
  y = 0;  y1 = 0;
  b[F_W1] += b[F_WS1];  b[F_A1] += b[F_AS1];  b[F_W2] += b[F_WS2];  b[F_A2] += b[F_AS2];
  lmd != 1 ? (                                                           // LINE 1
    d = b[F_I1] * (1 + jit * (rand(2) - 1));
    p = b[F_P1] + d;  p >= 1 ? ( p -= 1;  b[F_C1] = !b[F_C1]; );  b[F_P1] = p;
    w = w12 >= 0 && b[F_C1] ? w12 : w11;
    y1 = pdw(w, p, max(0, b[F_W1]), 2 * d);
    qz > 0 ? y1 = floor(y1 * qz + 0.5) / qz;                            // DRIFT: the table's rounding
    lmd != 1 ? y = y1 * b[F_A1];
  );
  lmd != 0 ? (                                                           // LINE 2 (1 + 1': line 1's waves, detuned)
    d = b[F_I2];
    nmod ? ( b[F_NZ] += ((rand(2) - 1) - b[F_NZ]) * 0.5;  d *= 1 + b[F_NZ] * 1.6; );   // NOISE: the pitch scrambled
    d *= 1 + jit * (rand(2) - 1);
    p = b[F_P2] + max(0, d);  p >= 1 ? ( p -= 1;  b[F_C2] = !b[F_C2]; );  b[F_P2] = p;
    ws = lmd == 3 ? w11 : w21;  w = lmd == 3 ? w12 : w22;
    w = w >= 0 && b[F_C2] ? w : ws;
    y2 = pdw(w, p, max(0, b[F_W2]), 2 * max(0.000001, d));
    qz > 0 ? y2 = floor(y2 * qz + 0.5) / qz;
    rmod ? y2 *= y1;                                                     // RING: line 2 x line 1
    y += y2 * b[F_A2];
  );
  // FILTER (TPT state-variable, at 2x)
  fmd ? (
    g = b[F_FG];  a1 = 1 / (1 + g * (g + b[F_FK]));
    v3 = y - b[F_FS2];  v1 = a1 * b[F_FS1] + g * a1 * v3;  v2 = b[F_FS2] + g * v1;
    b[F_FS1] = 2 * v1 - b[F_FS1];  b[F_FS2] = 2 * v2 - b[F_FS2];
    y = fmd == 1 ? v2 : fmd == 2 ? v1 * b[F_FK] : y - b[F_FK] * v1 - v2;
  );
  b[F_STEAL] ? (
    b[F_FADE] -= fade_s;
    b[F_FADE] <= 0 ? ( b[F_FADE] = 1;  b[F_STEAL] = 0;  b[F_A1] = 0;  b[F_A2] = 0;  b[F_AS1] = 0;  b[F_AS2] = 0;
      b[F_PEND] >= 0 ? v_start(b, b[F_PEND], b[F_PVEL]) : b[F_ON] = 0; );
    y *= b[F_FADE];
  );
  y;
);

function update_params() local(o, k) (
  drift_macro(drift);
  // the wave and line choices: a change dips the voices smoothly (6 ms), swaps, comes back (no click)
  n_lmd = floor(line_md + 0.5);  n_rmod = ring >= 0.5 && n_lmd != 0 && n_lmd != 1;  n_nmod = noise >= 0.5 && n_lmd != 0;
  n_w11 = floor(l1_w1 + 0.5);  n_w12 = floor(l1_w2 + 0.5) - 1;  n_w21 = floor(l2_w1 + 0.5);  n_w22 = floor(l2_w2 + 0.5) - 1;
  (n_lmd != lmd || n_rmod != rmod || n_nmod != nmod || n_w11 != w11 || n_w12 != w12 || n_w21 != w21 || n_w22 != w22) ? wv_pend = 1;
  det_st = floor(det_oct + 0.5) * 12 + floor(det_note + 0.5) + det_fine / 100;
  dkf[0] = l1_dkf / 100;  akf[0] = l1_akf / 100;  dkf[1] = l2_dkf / 100;  akf[1] = l2_akf / 100;
  n_lmd == 3 ? ( dkf[1] = dkf[0];  akf[1] = akf[0];  det_st = det_fine / 100 + floor(det_oct + 0.5) * 12 + floor(det_note + 0.5); );
  dcw_d = dcw_dep / 100;  vsn = vsens / 100;
  l2_g = 10 ^ (l2_lvl / 20);
  fmd = floor(flt_md + 0.5);  fkt = flt_kt / 100;              // (fcut, fk and fenv follow their knobs through the glide at the tick)
  fl_k = 1 - exp(-CR / (0.015 * srate));
  vib_d = vib_dep;  dcw_m = dcw_mod / 100 * 0.6;
  gl_c = glide <= 1.5 ? 1 : 1 - exp(-CR / (glide * 0.001 * srate * 0.5));     // GLIDE: about the set time to get most of the way
  n_mo = mono >= 0.5;  n_mo != mo_m ? ( v_all_off();  mo_m = n_mo; );
  fade_s = 1 / (0.003 * 2 * srate);  wdk_s = 1 / (0.006 * srate);
  dr_c = 1 - exp(-CR * dm_s / (1.5 * srate));
  jit = 0.0015 * dm_a;                                                   // DRIFT: phase jitter
  dtm_c = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.15 * srate));  ch_lpc = 1 - exp(-2 * $pi * 9000 / srate);
  out_t = 10 ^ (vol / 20);  sm_c = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.03 * srate));  sw_c = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.015 * srate));
  thk_lift = 0.5;  thk_drv = 0.4;  thk_asym = 0.1;  thk_tr = 0.3;  thk_trim = 0;
  // FX strip
  ph_inc = ph_rate / srate;  ph_d = ph_dep / 100;  ph_f = ph_fb / 100 * 0.9;
  ch_ia = 0.56 * ch_rate / srate;  ch_ib = 7.14 * ch_rate / srate;  ch_d = ch_dep / 100;  ch_m = ch_mix / 100;
  dr_g = 10 ^ (dr_amt / 100 * 30 / 20);  dr_k = 10 ^ (-dr_amt / 100 * 30 / 20 * 0.82);   // DRIVE: up to +30 dB in, level-matched out
  k = 1500 * 12 ^ (dr_tone / 100);  dr_lp = 1 - exp(-2 * $pi * min(k, 0.45 * srate) / srate);
  cp_t = cp_thr;  cp_r = 1 / max(cp_rat, 1);  cp_ac = 1 - exp(-1 / (cp_att * 0.001 * srate));  cp_rc = 1 - exp(-1 / (cp_rel * 0.001 * srate));
  cp_mk = 10 ^ (-cp_thr * (1 - cp_r) * 0.25 / 20);
  k = floor(dl_div + 0.5);
  dl_beats = k == 0 ? 0.125 : k == 1 ? 1 / 6 : k == 2 ? 0.25 : k == 3 ? 1 / 3 : k == 4 ? 0.375 : k == 5 ? 0.5 : k == 6 ? 2 / 3 : k == 7 ? 0.75 :
             k == 8 ? 1 : k == 9 ? 4 / 3 : k == 10 ? 1.5 : k == 11 ? 2 : 4;
  dl_fbg = dl_fb / 100;  dl_dc = 1 - exp(-2 * $pi * dl_damp / srate);  dl_mx = dl_mix / 100;
);
lmd = -1;  wdk = 1;  ms_n = 0;  mo_m = mono >= 0.5;
dkf = 1100;  akf = 1110;  EV = 1020;  PHS = 1120;  memset(PHS, 0, 16);
update_params();  fl_ok = 0;
dr_gs = dr_g;  dr_ks = dr_k;  cp_ts = cp_t;  cp_ms = cp_mk;  dl_ms_ = dl_mx;  dl_fs = dl_fbg;  ch_ms = ch_m;  ch_ds = ch_d;  ph_ds = ph_d;  ph_fs = ph_f;
lmd = n_lmd;  rmod = n_rmod;  nmod = n_nmod;  w11 = n_w11;  w12 = n_w12;  w21 = n_w21;  w22 = n_w22;  wv_pend = 0;
out_g = out_t;

clp_pf_on = 0;  dr_c.clp_set(1, 1, 1, 0);  dr_d.clp_set(1, 1, 1, 0);  dl_ts = 0.4 * srate;

// (moved here from @gfx: the PRESET parameter loads presets on the audio side)
function param_touched(idx) ( slider_automate(2 ^ (idx - 1));  gui_dirty = 1; );
function param_touched_au(idx) ( slider_automate(2 ^ (idx - 1));  gui_dirty = 1; );
function pv(i, v) ( slider(i) = v; );
function p_init() (
  pv(1, 0); pv(2, 0); pv(3, 0); pv(4, 0); pv(5, 0); pv(6, 0); pv(7, 0); pv(8, 0); pv(9, 0); pv(10, 0);
  pv(11, 30); pv(12, 30); pv(13, 30); pv(14, 30); pv(15, 100); pv(16, 0); pv(17, 0); pv(18, 8000); pv(19, 0); pv(20, 0); pv(21, 0);
  pv(22, 50); pv(23, 0); pv(24, 0.3); pv(25, 5); pv(26, 0); pv(27, 0); pv(28, 50); pv(30, 0);
  pv(31, 0); pv(32, 0.4); pv(33, 60); pv(34, 40); pv(35, 0); pv(36, 1); pv(37, 60); pv(38, 50); pv(39, 0); pv(40, 30); pv(41, 60);
  pv(42, 0); pv(43, -18); pv(44, 4); pv(45, 10); pv(46, 150); pv(47, 0); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 7); pv(50, 375); pv(51, 35); pv(52, 5000); pv(53, 25); pv(54, 0); pv(55, 80); pv(56, 0);
  env_default();
);
function load_preset(p) local(i) (
  p_init();
  p == 2 ? ( // GLASS BELL
    pv(27, -3.0); pv(1, 2); pv(2, 1); pv(4, 0); pv(6, 1); pv(8, 1); pv(9, 7); pv(10, 4); pv(16, -4); pv(11, 10); pv(13, 10); pv(12, 40); pv(14, 40); pv(35, 1); pv(38, 35); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 8); pv(51, 30); pv(53, 18);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 25, 30, 8, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(0, 2, 99, 99, 6, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 1, 99, 60, 20, 10, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 2, 99, 99, 10, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
  );
  p == 3 ? ( // PHASE STRINGS
    pv(27, -3.7); pv(1, 3); pv(4, 0); pv(10, 12); pv(35, 1); pv(37, 70); pv(38, 60); pv(26, 10); pv(24, 0.7); pv(25, 5.2);
    env_set(0, 1, 35, 55, 25, 38, 40, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 45, 99, 40, 90, 38, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 4 ? ( // ELECTRIC PIANO
    pv(27, 1.6); pv(1, 2); pv(4, 0); pv(6, 2); pv(8, 1); pv(16, -8); pv(22, 70); pv(35, 1); pv(38, 40); pv(13, 50);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 10, 30, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(0, 2, 99, 99, 20, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 1, 99, 70, 55, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 2, 99, 99, 45, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
  );
  p == 5 ? ( // BRASS LEAD
    pv(27, -3.2); pv(1, 0); pv(4, 0); pv(26, 15); pv(24, 0.5); pv(25, 5.5); pv(39, 1); pv(40, 20); pv(41, 55); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 7); pv(51, 25); pv(53, 15);
    env_set(0, 0, 99, 8, 70, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(0, 1, 60, 80, 50, 55, 40, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 70, 99, 50, 85, 55, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 6 ? ( // RESONANT SWEEP
    pv(27, -1.8); pv(1, 0); pv(4, 5); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 7); pv(51, 40); pv(53, 30);
    env_set(0, 1, 22, 99, 18, 15, 30, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 80, 99, 50, 90, 40, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 7 ? ( // AMBIENT PAD
    pv(27, 6); pv(1, 3); pv(4, 3); pv(5, 7); pv(10, 8); pv(31, 1); pv(32, 0.15); pv(33, 50); pv(34, 30); pv(35, 1); pv(38, 60); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 10); pv(51, 50); pv(53, 35);
    env_set(0, 1, 15, 60, 10, 30, 15, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 15, 99, 20, 80, 12, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 8 ? ( // METALLIC PLUCK
    pv(27, -1.6); pv(1, 2); pv(2, 1); pv(4, 2); pv(6, 0); pv(8, 1); pv(9, 4); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 5); pv(51, 30); pv(53, 25);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 90, 50, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(0, 2, 99, 99, 38, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 1, 99, 70, 45, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 2, 99, 99, 40, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
  );
  p == 9 ? ( // DIRTY SYNC BASS
    pv(27, -1.6); pv(1, 2); pv(4, 7); pv(6, 1); pv(8, -1); pv(16, -6); pv(11, 0); pv(13, 0); pv(39, 1); pv(40, 55); pv(41, 45); pv(42, 1); pv(43, -20); pv(44, 4);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 95, 55, 25, 60, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 99, 99, 60, 90, 65, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 1, 99, 40, 50, 20, 60, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 2, 99, 99, 60, 90, 65, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 10 ? ( // CHORUS ORGAN
    pv(27, -8.0); pv(1, 2); pv(4, 1); pv(6, 1); pv(8, 1); pv(16, -6); pv(35, 1); pv(36, 1.3); pv(37, 70); pv(38, 70);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 40, 50, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, 0, 1);
    env_set(0, 2, 99, 99, 80, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, 0, 1);
    env_set(1, 1, 99, 30, 50, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, 0, 1);
    env_set(1, 2, 99, 99, 80, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, 0, 1);
  );
  p == 11 ? ( // SCI-FI FX
    pv(27, 2.5); pv(1, 2); pv(3, 1); pv(4, 5); pv(6, 5); pv(8, 1); pv(31, 1); pv(32, 3); pv(33, 80); pv(34, 60); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 6); pv(51, 60); pv(53, 35);
    env_set(0, 0, 35, 99, 15, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(0, 1, 30, 99, 20, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(0, 2, 60, 99, 10, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 0, 30, 70, 20, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 1, 25, 99, 18, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 2, 60, 99, 10, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
  );
  p == 12 ? ( // SOFT EVOLUTION
    pv(27, -0.4); pv(1, 3); pv(4, 3); pv(5, 1); pv(10, 10); pv(35, 1); pv(38, 50); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 8); pv(51, 45); pv(53, 30);
    env_set(0, 1, 10, 70, 8, 20, 6, 60, 10, 0, 2, 3);
    env_set(0, 2, 8, 99, 10, 85, 8, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 13 ? ( // SYNTH BASS
    pv(27, 1.2); pv(1, 2); pv(4, 0); pv(6, 1); pv(8, -1); pv(16, -8); pv(11, 0); pv(13, 0); pv(22, 60); pv(42, 1); pv(43, -20); pv(44, 3);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 85, 45, 30, 50, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 99, 99, 60, 90, 70, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 1, 99, 10, 50, 10, 50, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 2, 99, 99, 60, 90, 70, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 14 ? ( // BREATHY FLUTE
    pv(27, 1.0); pv(1, 2); pv(3, 1); pv(4, 3); pv(6, 0); pv(16, -14); pv(26, 12); pv(24, 0.4); pv(25, 5); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 7); pv(51, 25); pv(53, 15);
    env_set(0, 1, 50, 20, 50, 12, 50, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 60, 99, 50, 85, 55, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 1, 70, 40, 50, 25, 50, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 2, 70, 99, 40, 30, 55, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 15 ? ( // FUNKY CLAV
    pv(27, -2.1); pv(1, 0); pv(4, 2); pv(22, 80); pv(12, 50); pv(39, 1); pv(40, 20); pv(41, 65);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 90, 40, 15, 60, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 99, 99, 30, 60, 85, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 16 ? ( // VIBES
    pv(27, 0.1); pv(1, 2); pv(4, 3); pv(6, 0); pv(8, 2); pv(16, -12); pv(11, 20); pv(22, 70); pv(35, 1); pv(36, 0.5); pv(37, 50); pv(38, 40);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 15, 30, 5, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(0, 2, 99, 99, 12, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 1, 99, 40, 40, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 2, 99, 99, 35, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
  );
  p == 17 ? ( // RESO LEAD
    pv(27, -2.0); pv(1, 3); pv(4, 6); pv(10, 7); pv(26, 18); pv(24, 0.5); pv(25, 5.5); pv(39, 1); pv(40, 15); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 7); pv(51, 30); pv(53, 20);
    env_set(0, 1, 70, 85, 45, 60, 50, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 90, 99, 50, 90, 60, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 18 ? ( // SYNC LEAD
    pv(27, -5.5); pv(1, 3); pv(4, 5); pv(5, 2); pv(10, 6); pv(26, 14); pv(24, 0.6); pv(25, 6); pv(39, 1); pv(40, 30); pv(41, 55); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 5); pv(51, 35); pv(53, 22);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 99, 55, 40, 50, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 99, 99, 50, 90, 60, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 19 ? ( // DIGITAL CHOIR
    pv(27, -1.9); pv(1, 2); pv(4, 7); pv(6, 3); pv(10, 9); pv(16, -3); pv(11, 50); pv(26, 8); pv(24, 0.8); pv(25, 4.8); pv(35, 1); pv(37, 70); pv(38, 60); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 8); pv(51, 35); pv(53, 20);
    env_set(0, 1, 30, 40, 20, 30, 40, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 25, 99, 30, 90, 30, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 1, 30, 30, 20, 20, 40, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 2, 25, 99, 30, 90, 30, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 20 ? ( // TUBULAR BELLS
    pv(27, -2.7); pv(1, 2); pv(2, 1); pv(4, 0); pv(6, 0); pv(8, 2); pv(10, 18); pv(16, -6); pv(11, 10); pv(13, 10); pv(12, 20); pv(14, 20); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 8); pv(51, 30); pv(53, 20);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 20, 30, 5, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(0, 2, 99, 99, 8, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 1, 99, 50, 25, 10, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 2, 99, 99, 12, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
  );
  p == 21 ? ( // MARIMBA
    pv(27, 5.7); pv(1, 2); pv(4, 3); pv(6, 0); pv(8, 2); pv(16, -10); pv(22, 80); pv(12, 50); pv(14, 50);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 30, 60, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(0, 2, 99, 99, 40, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 1, 99, 60, 70, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(1, 2, 99, 99, 70, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
  );
  p == 22 ? ( // HARPSICHORD
    pv(27, -5.0); pv(1, 3); pv(4, 4); pv(10, 5); pv(11, 20); pv(12, 60); pv(22, 30); pv(35, 1); pv(36, 0.7); pv(37, 40); pv(38, 30);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 95, 30, 35, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
    env_set(0, 2, 99, 99, 22, 0, 50, 0, 50, 0, -1, 1);
  );
  p == 23 ? ( // RESO BASS
    pv(27, 3.2); pv(1, 2); pv(4, 5); pv(6, 1); pv(8, -1); pv(16, -6); pv(11, 0); pv(13, 0); pv(22, 60); pv(39, 1); pv(40, 35); pv(41, 50); pv(42, 1); pv(43, -20); pv(44, 4);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 90, 50, 20, 50, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 99, 99, 60, 85, 70, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 1, 99, 10, 50, 10, 50, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 2, 99, 99, 60, 85, 70, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 24 ? ( // NIGHT WIND
    pv(27, 3.8); pv(1, 2); pv(3, 1); pv(4, 3); pv(6, 5); pv(8, 1); pv(16, 0); pv(31, 1); pv(32, 0.1); pv(33, 70); pv(34, 50); pv(35, 1); pv(38, 50); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 11); pv(51, 55); pv(53, 35);
    env_set(0, 1, 20, 30, 20, 20, 30, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 20, 99, 15, 90, 12, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 1, 8, 80, 6, 20, 8, 70, 10, 0, 2, 3);
    env_set(1, 2, 20, 99, 15, 90, 12, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 25 ? ( // SPACE CHOIR
    pv(27, -1.7); pv(1, 2); pv(4, 0); pv(6, 2); pv(10, 10); pv(16, -2); pv(11, 40); pv(13, 40); pv(23, 0); pv(24, 1.2); pv(25, 1.2); pv(26, 4); pv(56, 40); pv(35, 1); pv(37, 75); pv(38, 65); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 11); pv(51, 50); pv(53, 35);
    env_set(0, 1, 20, 30, 18, 55, 14, 70, 30, 0, 2, 3);
    env_set(0, 2, 12, 99, 20, 90, 10, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 1, 18, 25, 16, 45, 12, 60, 30, 0, 2, 3);
    env_set(1, 2, 12, 99, 20, 90, 10, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 26 ? ( // SYNTH STRINGS
    pv(27, -3.4); pv(1, 2); pv(4, 0); pv(6, 6); pv(8, 1); pv(10, 4); pv(16, -5); pv(28, 70); pv(24, 0.6); pv(25, 5.5); pv(26, 8); pv(35, 1); pv(37, 55); pv(38, 45); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 8); pv(51, 25); pv(53, 15);
    env_set(0, 1, 55, 70, 40, 45, 45, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 55, 99, 50, 95, 45, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 1, 60, 85, 35, 40, 45, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 2, 60, 99, 35, 55, 45, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  p == 27 ? ( // SPACE FLUTE
    pv(27, 4.9); pv(54, 1); pv(55, 140); pv(1, 2); pv(3, 1); pv(4, 0); pv(6, 2); pv(16, -12); pv(11, 20); pv(24, 0.5); pv(25, 5.2); pv(26, 14); pv(47, 1); pv(48, 1); pv(49, 7); pv(51, 35); pv(52, 3500); pv(53, 25);
    env_set(0, 1, 99, 60, 70, 12, 50, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(0, 2, 85, 99, 50, 90, 75, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 1, 99, 40, 60, 20, 50, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
    env_set(1, 2, 99, 70, 60, 15, 70, 0, 50, 0, 1, 2);
  );
  i = 1;  loop(56, i != 29 ? param_touched_au(i);  i += 1; );
);

// PRESET parameter (JG, 28 Oct 2026: accessibility - a screen reader reaches the presets through REAPER's parameter list).
// A change of prs_sel (a screen reader, the host, automation) loads that preset (0 = No preset: nothing loaded); the preset bar asks through
// prs_dirty. Both load here, on the audio side only. prs_last is saved, so opening a project or recalling its
// state never reloads a preset over the saved settings.
function prs_chk() local(k) (
  prs_dirty > 0 ? (
    k = prs_dirty; prs_dirty = 0; load_preset(k);
    k <= 27 ? ( prs_sel = k; slider_automate(prs_sel); prs_cur_d = k; );
    prs_last = prs_sel;
  ) : prs_ok ? (
    prs_sel = max(0, min(27, prs_sel | 0));
    prs_sel != prs_last ? ( prs_last = prs_sel; prs_sel > 0 ? ( load_preset(prs_sel); prs_cur_d = prs_sel; ); );
  ) : ( prs_last = prs_sel | 0; prs_ok = 1; );
);
prs_ok = 0; prs_dirty = 0;

@slider
prs_chk();
update_params();

@block
prs_chk();
mq_n = 0;
while (mq_n < MQMAX && midirecv(m_ofs, m_st, m_d1, m_d2)) (
  MQ[mq_n * 4] = m_ofs;  MQ[mq_n * 4 + 1] = m_st;  MQ[mq_n * 4 + 2] = m_d1;  MQ[mq_n * 4 + 3] = m_d2;
  mq_n += 1;  midisend(m_ofs, m_st, m_d1 + m_d2 * 256);
);
mq_i = 0;  spos = 0;
tp_now = play_state & 1;  tp_was && !tp_now ? v_all_off();  tp_was = tp_now;
prm_dirty ? ( prm_dirty = 0;  update_params(); );
// DRIFT: the table's rounding wanders (about 11 bits at 50 %), the output warms and cools
dq = dr_q.drift_tick(0.3 * samplesblock / srate * dm_s);
qz = dm_a > 0.001 ? 2 ^ (14.2 - 1.2 * dm_a + dq * 0.5 * dm_a) : 0;    // about 13 bits at 50 %, 12 at 100 %
th_g = 1 + dr_t.drift_tick(0.15 * samplesblock / srate * dm_s) * 0.029 * dm_a;
vib_inc = vib_rate / srate;
dl_tt = min(DLN - 4, (dl_sync >= 0.5 ? dl_beats * 60 / max(tempo, 20) : dl_ms * 0.001) * srate);
dr_c.clp_set(1, 1, 1, 0);  dr_d.clp_set(1, 1, 1, 0);
ost_setup(0, 0.3, 120, 6000, -0.3, 1);                                 // house output stage: CLIP
outpk_disp = max(outpk_disp, outpk);  outpk = 0;  gr_disp = max(gr_disp, cp_grd);  cp_grd = 0;
k = 0;  loop(NV, VD[k] = VOX[k * VS + F_ON] ? max(VOX[k * VS + F_A1], VOX[k * VS + F_A2]) : 0;  k += 1; );
// the envelope display follows the newest voice
vn_b = -1;  vn_a = -1;  k = 0;  loop(NV, VOX[k * VS + F_ON] && VOX[k * VS + F_AGE] > vn_a ? ( vn_a = VOX[k * VS + F_AGE];  vn_b = VOX + k * VS; );  k += 1; );
vn_b >= 0 ? ( k = 0;  loop(6, EV[k * 2] = vn_b[F_EN + k * 4];  EV[k * 2 + 1] = vn_b[F_EN + k * 4 + 1];  k += 1; );  ev_on_d = 1; ) : ev_on_d = 0;

@serialize
file_var(0, pr_cur);
file_var(0, ui_sz);
file_var(0, env_ok);
file_mem(0, E, 6 * ES);
file_avail(0) != 0 ? file_var(0, prs_last) : prs_last = prs_sel | 0; prs_ok = 1;   // PRESET parameter: no reload on recall

@sample
while (mq_i < mq_n && MQ[mq_i * 4] <= spos) ( midi_event(mq_i);  mq_i += 1; );
spos += 1;
cr_n <= 0 ? (
  cr_n = CR;
  // FILTER: CUTOFF, RESO and ENV glide (two 15 ms stages on the cutoff, 15 ms on the rest), so a turned knob never steps
  !fl_ok ? ( fl_c1 = fl_c2 = log(flt_cut);  fl_rs = flt_res;  fl_ev = flt_env / 100;  fl_ok = 1; );
  fl_c1 += (log(flt_cut) - fl_c1) * fl_k;  fl_c2 += (fl_c1 - fl_c2) * fl_k;  fl_rs += (flt_res - fl_rs) * fl_k;  fl_ev += (flt_env / 100 - fl_ev) * fl_k;
  fcut = exp(fl_c2);  fk = 2 - fl_rs / 100 * 1.94;  fenv = fl_ev;
  // VIBRATO: one LFO for every voice
  vib_ph += vib_inc * CR;  vib_ph -= floor(vib_ph);
  vwv = floor(vib_wv + 0.5);
  vib_v = vwv == 0 ? 1 - 4 * abs(vib_ph - 0.5) : vwv == 1 ? 2 * vib_ph - 1 : vwv == 2 ? 1 - 2 * vib_ph : (vib_ph < 0.5 ? 1 : -1);
  vb = VOX;  loop(NV, vb[F_ON] ? v_tick(vb);  vb += VS; );
);
cr_n -= 1;

// the voices at twice the sample rate, then down through the half-band
s0 = 0;  s1 = 0;
vb = VOX;  loop(NV, vb[F_ON] ? ( s0 += v_run(vb);  s1 += v_run(vb); );  vb += VS; );
HB[64 + hb_w] = s0;  HB[64 + 64 + hb_w] = s0;  hb_w = (hb_w + 1) & 63;
HB[64 + hb_w] = s1;  HB[64 + 64 + hb_w] = s1;  hb_w = (hb_w + 1) & 63;
hb_y = 0;  hb_k = 0;  hb_p = HB + 64 + hb_w;                            // (a mirrored history: the 63 newest in a row)
hb_y = HB[31] * hb_p[32];  loop(16, hb_y += HB[hb_k] * (hb_p[hb_k + 1] + hb_p[63 - hb_k]);  hb_k += 2; );   // (half the taps are zero; it's symmetric)
y = hb_y * 0.16 * wdk * wdk * (3 - 2 * wdk);                                                 // TWEAK: the voice level (x the change dip)
wv_pend ? ( wdk -= wdk_s;  wdk <= 0 ? ( wdk = 0;  lmd = n_lmd;  rmod = n_rmod;  nmod = n_nmod;  w11 = n_w11;  w12 = n_w12;  w21 = n_w21;  w22 = n_w22;  wv_pend = 0; ); )
        : wdk = min(1, wdk + wdk_s);

// DC blocker (5 Hz): the pulse and resonance waves carry DC
dc_x = y - dc_p + dc_r * dc_x;  dc_p = y;  y = dc_x;
yl = y;  yr = y;
// ---------- FX STRIP ----------
// the strip's gains glide (30 ms): a preset or a knob never jumps them
dr_gs += (dr_g - dr_gs) * sm_c;  dr_ks += (dr_k - dr_ks) * sm_c;  cp_ts += (cp_t - cp_ts) * sm_c;  cp_ms += (cp_mk - cp_ms) * sm_c;
dl_ms_ += (dl_mx - dl_ms_) * sm_c;  dl_fs += (dl_fbg - dl_fs) * sm_c;  ch_ms += (ch_m - ch_ms) * sm_c;  ch_ds += (ch_d - ch_ds) * sm_c;  ph_ds += (ph_d - ph_ds) * sm_c;  ph_fs += (ph_f - ph_fs) * sm_c;
phx += ((ph_on >= 0.5) - phx) * sw_c;  chx += ((ch_on >= 0.5) - chx) * sw_c;  drx += ((dr_on >= 0.5) - drx) * sw_c;
cpx += ((cp_on >= 0.5) - cpx) * sw_c;  dlx += ((dl_on >= 0.5) - dlx) * sw_c;
// PHASER: 6 first-order all-passes swept from 200 Hz to 4 kHz (DEPTH), feedback round them; left and right 90 degrees apart
phx > 0.0001 ? (
  ph_p += ph_inc;  ph_p -= floor(ph_p);
  g_a = 200 * 20 ^ (ph_ds * (0.5 + 0.5 * sin(2 * $pi * ph_p)));  g_b = 200 * 20 ^ (ph_ds * (0.5 + 0.5 * cos(2 * $pi * ph_p)));
  g_a = tan($pi * g_a / srate);  g_a = (g_a - 1) / (g_a + 1);  g_b = tan($pi * g_b / srate);  g_b = (g_b - 1) / (g_b + 1);
  u = yl + phl_fb * ph_fs;  k = 0;  loop(6, t = g_a * u + PHS[k];  PHS[k] = u - g_a * t;  u = t;  k += 1; );  phl_fb = u;
  yl = yl + (u - yl) * 0.5 * phx;
  u = yr + phr_fb * ph_fs;  k = 0;  loop(6, t = g_b * u + PHS[8 + k];  PHS[8 + k] = u - g_b * t;  u = t;  k += 1; );  phr_fb = u;
  yr = yr + (u - yr) * 0.5 * phx;
) : ph_z ? ( memset(PHS, 0, 16);  phl_fb = 0;  phr_fb = 0;  ph_z = 0; );    // out: it starts clean next time
phx > 0.0001 ? ph_z = 1;
// CHORUS: the original's three BBD lines (2 - 7 ms), a three-phase LFO - 0.56 Hz and 7.14 Hz mixed 10:1
CHB[ch_w] = (yl + yr) * 0.5;                                           // (the line is kept fresh while the chorus is out)
chx > 0.0001 ? (
  ch_pa += ch_ia;  ch_pa -= floor(ch_pa);  ch_pb += ch_ib;  ch_pb -= floor(ch_pb);
  k = 0;  c_l = 0;  c_r = 0;
  loop(3,
    t = (abs(2 * frac3(ch_pa + k / 3) - 1) * 10 + abs(2 * frac3(ch_pb + k / 3) - 1)) / 11;   // two triangles, 120 degrees apart per line
    d = (2.2 + (2 + 3 * t) * ch_ds) * 0.001 * srate;
    u = ch_w - d;  u < 0 ? u += CHN;  i = floor(u);  f = u - i;  j = i + 1;  j >= CHN ? j = 0;
    u = CHB[i] + (CHB[j] - CHB[i]) * f;
    k == 0 ? c_l += u : k == 1 ? ( c_l += u * 0.5;  c_r += u * 0.5; ) : c_r += u;
    k += 1; );
  ch_lp1 += (c_l - ch_lp1) * ch_lpc;  ch_lp2 += (c_r - ch_lp2) * ch_lpc;                       // the BBD's darker top
  yl += ch_lp1 * 0.75 * ch_ms * chx;  yr += ch_lp2 * 0.75 * ch_ms * chx;
  yl *= 1 - 0.25 * ch_ms * chx;  yr *= 1 - 0.25 * ch_ms * chx;
);
ch_w += 1;  ch_w >= CHN ? ch_w = 0;
// DRIVE: the house soft clipper (anti-aliased), level-matched, then TONE
drx > 0.0001 ? (
  u = dr_c.clp_run(yl * dr_gs) * dr_ks;  t = dr_d.clp_run(yr * dr_gs) * dr_ks;
  dr_l += (u - dr_l) * dr_lp;  dr_r += (t - dr_r) * dr_lp;
  yl += (dr_l - yl) * drx;  yr += (dr_r - yr) * drx;
);
// COMP: stereo-linked, its level in dB with ATTACK / RELEASE, a 6 dB soft knee, automatic make-up
cpx > 0.0001 ? (
  u = max(abs(yl), abs(yr));  u = u > 0.000001 ? 20 * log10(u) : -120;
  t = u - cp_ts;  t = t < -3 ? 0 : t > 3 ? t : (t + 3) * (t + 3) / 12;                                   // over the threshold (knee)
  t = t * (1 - cp_r);
  cp_env += (t - cp_env) * (t > cp_env ? cp_ac : cp_rc);
  cp_gr_ = cp_env;  u = 10 ^ (-cp_env / 20) * cp_ms;
  yl += (yl * u - yl) * cpx;  yr += (yr * u - yr) * cpx;
);
cp_grd = max(cp_grd, cp_gr_ * cpx);
// DELAY: a note value or ms (glided), FEEDBACK through DAMPING and a soft limit in the loop, MIX
dlx > 0.0001 || dl_tail > 0.00001 ? (
  dl_ts += (dl_tt - dl_ts) * dtm_c;
  u = dl_w - dl_ts;  u < 0 ? u += DLN;  i = floor(u);  f = u - i;  j = i + 1;  j >= DLN ? j = 0;
  el = DLB[i] + (DLB[j] - DLB[i]) * f;  er = DLB[DLN + i] + (DLB[DLN + j] - DLB[DLN + i]) * f;
  dl_fl += (el - dl_fl) * dl_dc;  dl_fr += (er - dl_fr) * dl_dc;
  DLB[dl_w] = ts(((yl + yr) * 0.5 * dlx + dl_fr * dl_fs) * 1.1) / 1.1;  DLB[DLN + dl_w] = ts(dl_fl * dl_fs * 1.1) / 1.1;   // ping-pong: in on the left, the repeats cross
  yl += el * dl_ms_;  yr += er * dl_ms_;
  dl_tail = max(abs(el), abs(er)) * 0.002 + dl_tail * 0.998;
) : ( DLB[dl_w] = 0;  DLB[DLN + dl_w] = 0; );
dl_w += 1;  dl_w >= DLN ? dl_w = 0;
// THICK (the house circuit) and the IN fade
thk_proc(yl, yr, thick >= 0.5);  yl = thk_l;  yr = thk_r;
in_x += ((in_on >= 0.5) - in_x) * sw_c;
out_g += (out_t * th_g - out_g) * sm_c;
yl *= out_g * in_x;  yr *= out_g * in_x;
ost_out(yl, yr);  yl = ost_l;  yr = ost_r;
outpk = max(outpk, max(abs(yl), abs(yr)));
spl0 = yl;  spl1 = yr;

@gfx 1200 902
// version tag (JG, 29 Oct 2026): v1 = Legacy, v2 = Stable, v3 = the next graduation; a small dim tag just after the
// panel title. ver_tag_at draws it at x with its baseline at yb, fs px high, in col (or the current colour if col < 0),
// at 55 %; ver_tag puts it after text just drawn (dx, dy: extra offset in that text's heights). Font, colour and
// gfx_x / gfx_y are left as they were.
function ver_tag_at(s, slot, x, yb, fs, col) local(x0, y0, r, g, b, a, f) (
  x0 = gfx_x; y0 = gfx_y; r = gfx_r; g = gfx_g; b = gfx_b; a = gfx_a; f = gfx_getfont();
  col >= 0 ? ( gfx_r = (col >> 16) / 255; gfx_g = ((col >> 8) & 255) / 255; gfx_b = (col & 255) / 255; gfx_a = 1; );
  gfx_setfont(slot, "Trebuchet MS", max(10, fs), 'b');
  gfx_x = x; gfx_y = yb - 0.8 * gfx_texth; gfx_a *= 0.55; gfx_drawstr(s);
  gfx_r = r; gfx_g = g; gfx_b = b; gfx_a = a; gfx_x = x0; gfx_y = y0; gfx_setfont(f + 1);
);
function ver_tag(s, slot, dx, dy) local(th) (
  th = gfx_texth;
  ver_tag_at(s, slot, gfx_x + (0.3 + dx) * th, gfx_y + (0.8 + dy) * th, 0.5 * th, -1);
);
// =====================================================================
// GUI - CZ77: a metallic gunmetal-grey faceplate, white silk-screened print, pointer knobs, cream selector keys, an
// amber pilot lamp, the small square grey THICK key with its red LED.
// =====================================================================
C_FACE = 0x4A4F55;  C_SEC1 = 0x535860;  C_SEC2 = 0x4F545B;  C_SEC3 = 0x575C63;
C_INK = 0xF2F3F2;  C_INK2 = 0xB9BFC5;  C_TEAL = 0xC8CDD2;  C_RULE = 0xE4E7EA;  C_TAB = 0x8FB8E0;
C_LCDBG = 0x0E130A;  C_LCDTX = 0xC6E878;
LK_YEL = 0xF2C230;  LK_AMB = 0xF2A41E;  LK_RED = 0xF0503A;  lk_well = 0x0E0F10;
function text_r(x, y, str) local(w, h) ( gfx_measurestr(str, w, h);  gfx_x = x - w;  gfx_y = y - h * 0.5;  gfx_drawstr(str); );
function col(h, a) ( gfx_r = floor(h / 65536) / 255;  gfx_g = (floor(h / 256) % 256) / 255;  gfx_b = (h % 256) / 255;  gfx_a = a; );
function shade(h, f) local(r, g, b) (
  r = min(255, floor(floor(h / 65536) * f));  g = min(255, floor((floor(h / 256) % 256) * f));  b = min(255, floor((h % 256) * f));
  r * 65536 + g * 256 + b;
);
function ui_mix(c1, c2, t) (
  floor(floor(c1 / 65536) * (1 - t) + floor(c2 / 65536) * t) * 65536 +
  floor((floor(c1 / 256) % 256) * (1 - t) + (floor(c2 / 256) % 256) * t) * 256 + floor((c1 % 256) * (1 - t) + (c2 % 256) * t);
);
function px(v) ( ox + v * sc; );
YS = 1.1;                                // the panel is laid out on 1200 x 820 and stretched 10 % taller: more room between rows
function py(v) ( oy + v * YS * sc; );
function ps(v) ( v * sc; );
function u_rect(x, y, w, h) ( gfx_rect(px(x), py(y), ps(w), ps(h) * YS, 1); );
function text_c(x, y, str) local(w, h) ( gfx_measurestr(str, w, h);  gfx_x = x - w * 0.5;  gfx_y = y - h * 0.5;  gfx_drawstr(str); );
function text_l(x, y, str) local(w, h) ( gfx_measurestr(str, w, h);  gfx_x = x;  gfx_y = y - h * 0.5;  gfx_drawstr(str); );
function shd_r(x, y, w, h) local(i) ( i = 0;  loop(4, col(0x000000, 0.13);  u_rect(x + 2 + i * 1.3, y + 3 + i * 1.6, w + i * 0.6, h + i * 0.6);  i += 1; ); );
function shd_c(cx, cy, r) local(i) ( i = 0;  loop(4, col(0x000000, 0.13);  gfx_circle(px(cx + 2 + i * 1.2), py(cy + 3 + i * 1.5), ps(r + i * 0.6), 1, 1);  i += 1; ); );
function rivet(x, y) ( col(0x5A5B5E, 1);  gfx_circle(px(x), py(y), ps(4), 1, 1);  col(0x8A8C90, 1);  gfx_circle(px(x) - ps(1), py(y) - ps(1), ps(1.4), 1, 1); );
// weathering: faint scuffs and stains, painted once into image 121 (again on resize)
function section(x, y, w, h, c, title) (
  shd_r(x, y, w, h);
  col(c, 1);  u_rect(x, y, w, h);
  col(shade(c, 0.7), 1);  u_rect(x, y + h - 2, w, 2);  u_rect(x + w - 2, y, 2, h);
  col(0xFFFFFF, 0.1);  u_rect(x, y, w - 2, 1);
  col(C_RULE, 0.75);  u_rect(x + 16, y + 34, w - 32, 2);
  gfx_setfont(4);  col(C_INK, 1);  text_l(px(x + 16), py(y + 19), title);
);
// dot pointer (JG, 31 Oct 2026: dial indicators are dots, not lines): a round dot on the cap, centre at 62 % of
// the cap radius capr, radius 19 % of it
function pdot(x, y, sa, ca, capr) ( gfx_circle(x + sa * capr * 0.62, y - ca * capr * 0.62, capr * 0.19, 1, 1); );
// automation above slider 63 goes by name
function pointer(x, y, sa, ca, r0, r1, hw) local(ax, ay, bx, by, dx, dy) (
  ax = x + sa * r0;  ay = y - ca * r0;  bx = x + sa * r1;  by = y - ca * r1;  dx = ca * hw;  dy = sa * hw;
  gfx_triangle(ax + dx, ay + dy, bx + dx, by + dy, bx - dx, by - dy, ax - dx, ay - dy);
  gfx_line(ax + dx, ay + dy, bx + dx, by + dy, 1);  gfx_line(ax - dx, ay - dy, bx - dx, by - dy, 1);
);
function fmtv(v, fmt) (
  fmt == 1 ? sprintf(#kv, "%d %%", v) :
  fmt == 2 ? sprintf(#kv, "%.1f Hz", v) :
  fmt == 3 ? sprintf(#kv, "%+.1f st", v) :
  fmt == 4 ? sprintf(#kv, "%+.1f dB", v) :
  fmt == 5 ? sprintf(#kv, "%.1f c", v) :
  fmt == 7 ? sprintf(#kv, "%.2f Hz", v) :
  fmt == 10 ? sprintf(#kv, "%+.2f oct", v) :
  fmt == 13 ? sprintf(#kv, "x %.2f", v) :
  fmt == 14 ? sprintf(#kv, "%.1f : 1", v) :
  fmt == 15 ? ( v < 10 ? sprintf(#kv, "%.1f ms", v) : sprintf(#kv, "%d ms", floor(v + 0.5)); ) :
  fmt == 16 ? ( v = floor(v + 0.5);  strcpy(#kv, v == 0 ? "1/32" : v == 1 ? "1/16 T" : v == 2 ? "1/16" : v == 3 ? "1/8 T" : v == 4 ? "1/16 D" : v == 5 ? "1/8" : v == 6 ? "1/4 T" : v == 7 ? "1/8 D" : v == 8 ? "1/4" : v == 9 ? "1/2 T" : v == 10 ? "1/4 D" : v == 11 ? "1/2" : "1 bar"); ) :
  fmt == 11 ? sprintf(#kv, "%.1f s", v) :
  fmt == 12 ? sprintf(#kv, "+%d ms", floor(v + 0.5)) :
  fmt == 9 ? ( v >= 1000 ? sprintf(#kv, "%.1f kHz", v / 1000) : sprintf(#kv, "%d Hz", floor(v + 0.5)); ) :
  fmt == 8 ? ( v < 1 ? sprintf(#kv, "%d ms", floor(v * 1000 + 0.5)) : sprintf(#kv, "%.2f s", v); ) :
  fmt == 6 ? ( v = floor(v + 0.5);  strcpy(#kv, v == 0 ? "1/32" : v == 1 ? "1/16" : v == 2 ? "1/8 T" : v == 3 ? "1/8" : v == 4 ? "1/4 T" :
              v == 5 ? "1/8 D" : v == 6 ? "1/4" : v == 7 ? "1/2" : "1 bar"); ) :
  sprintf(#kv, "%.2f", v);
  #kv;
);
function hover_tag(x, y, str) local(w, h) (
  gfx_setfont(3);  gfx_measurestr(str, w, h);
  col(C_LCDBG, 0.95);  gfx_rect(x - w * 0.5 - ps(6), y - h * 0.5 - ps(3), w + ps(12), h + ps(6), 1);
  col(C_LCDTX, 1);  text_c(x, y, str);
);
// big industrial pointer knob: a knurled black skirt, a dark cap, a white pointer bar; teal and white scale
function kn(cx, cy, r, idx, vmin, vmax, def, lbl, fmt) local(x, y, rr, v, t, hov, now, a0, a1, tv, b, j, lgt, st)
(
  lgt = klog;  klog = 0;  st = kstep;  kstep = 0;
  x = px(cx);  y = py(cy);  rr = ps(r);
  hov = sqr(mouse_x - x) + sqr(mouse_y - y) <= sqr(rr * 1.2);
  v = max(vmin, min(vmax, slider(idx)));
  t = lgt ? log(v / vmin) / log(vmax / vmin) : (v - vmin) / (vmax - vmin);
  click && hov && !drag_idx ? (
    now = time_precise();
    (mouse_cap & 4) || (last_click_idx == idx && now - last_click_t < 0.3) ? ( slider(idx) = def;  param_touched(idx);  drag_idx = 0; )
                                                                           : ( drag_idx = idx;  drag_y = mouse_y;  drag_t = t; );
    last_click_idx = idx;  last_click_t = now;
  );
  hov && mouse_wheel != 0 && !drag_idx ? (
    st > 0 ? v = max(vmin, min(vmax, v + sign(mouse_wheel) * st)) : (
      t = max(0, min(1, t + mouse_wheel / 120 * ((mouse_cap & 8) ? 0.005 : 0.03)));
      v = lgt ? vmin * exp(t * log(vmax / vmin)) : vmin + t * (vmax - vmin);
    );
    v != slider(idx) ? ( slider(idx) = v;  param_touched(idx); );
    mouse_wheel = 0;
  );
  drag_idx == idx ? (
    t = max(0, min(1, drag_t + (drag_y - mouse_y) / ps((mouse_cap & 8) ? 1100 : 220)));
    v = lgt ? vmin * exp(t * log(vmax / vmin)) : vmin + t * (vmax - vmin);
    st > 0 ? v = vmin + floor((v - vmin) / st + 0.5) * st : v = floor(v * 10 + 0.5) / 10;
    v = max(vmin, min(vmax, v));
    v != slider(idx) ? ( slider(idx) = v;  param_touched(idx); );
  );
  v = max(vmin, min(vmax, slider(idx)));
  t = lgt ? log(v / vmin) / log(vmax / vmin) : (v - vmin) / (vmax - vmin);
  a0 = -0.75 * $pi;  a1 = 0.75 * $pi;  tv = a0 + t * (a1 - a0);
  j = 0;
  loop(21,
    b = a0 + j / 20 * (a1 - a0);  col(j % 5 == 0 ? C_INK : C_TEAL, j % 5 == 0 ? 0.95 : 0.6);
    gfx_circle((x + sin(b) * (rr + ps(6) + rr + ps(j % 5 == 0 ? 14 : 10)) * 0.5), (y - cos(b) * (rr + ps(6) + rr + ps(j % 5 == 0 ? 14 : 10)) * 0.5), max(((rr + ps(j % 5 == 0 ? 14 : 10)) - (rr + ps(6))) * 0.25, 1), 1, 1);
    j += 1;
  );
  shd_c(cx, cy, r);
  col(0x141516, 1);  gfx_circle(x, y, rr, 1, 1);
  j = 0;  loop(36, b = j / 36 * 2 * $pi;  col(0x3A3C3E, 1);  gfx_line(x + sin(b) * rr * 0.86, y - cos(b) * rr * 0.86, x + sin(b) * rr * 0.98, y - cos(b) * rr * 0.98, 1);  j += 1; );
  col(0x2A2B2D, 1);  gfx_circle(x, y, rr * 0.8, 1, 1);
  col(0xFFFFFF, 0.08);  gfx_arc(x, y, rr * 0.74, -1.8, -0.1, 1);
  col(C_INK, 1);  pdot(x, y, sin(tv), cos(tv), rr * 0.8);
  gfx_setfont(6);  col(C_INK, 1);  text_c(x, y + rr + ps(19), lbl);
  hov || drag_idx == idx ? hover_tag(x, y - rr - ps(22), fmtv(v, fmt));
);
function ui_rrs(x, y, w, h, r) local(i, d, ins) (
  x = floor(x + 0.5); y = floor(y + 0.5); w = floor(w + 0.5); h = floor(h + 0.5);
  r = min(floor(r + 0.5), floor(min(w, h) * 0.5));
  i = 0;
  loop(r, d = r - i - 0.5; ins = floor(r - sqrt(max(r * r - d * d, 0)) + 0.5);
    gfx_rect(x + ins, y + i, w - 2 * ins, 1);  gfx_rect(x + ins, y + h - 1 - i, w - 2 * ins, 1);  i += 1; );
  gfx_rect(x, y + r, w, h - 2 * r);
);
function lk_rr(x, y, w, h, r) ( ui_rrs(px(x), py(y), ps(w), ps(h) * YS, ps(r)); );
function ui_keytext(cx, cy, str) local(w, h) ( gfx_measurestr(str, w, h); gfx_x = floor(cx - w * 0.5 + 0.5); gfx_y = floor(cy - h * 0.58 + 0.5); gfx_drawstr(str); );
function lk_key(x, y, w, h, on, c, str) local(hov, hit, k, lens, dn, i, t, dx, dy) (
  hov = mouse_x >= px(x) && mouse_x < px(x + w) && mouse_y >= py(y) && mouse_y < py(y + h);
  hit = click && hov && !drag_idx;
  dn = hov && lmb ? 1 : 0;
  k = min(w / 54, h / 40);
  lens = shade(ui_mix(c, 0xCFC9BC, 0.5), 0.76);
  on ? lens = c;
  on ? ( col(c, 0.10); lk_rr(x - 9 * k, y - 9 * k, w + 18 * k, h + 18 * k, 10 * k);  col(c, 0.18); lk_rr(x - 6 * k, y - 6 * k, w + 12 * k, h + 12 * k, 8 * k); );
  col(lk_well, 1);           lk_rr(x - 4 * k, y - 4 * k, w + 8 * k, h + 8 * k, 5 * k);
  col(shade(lens, 0.55), 1); lk_rr(x, y + 1 / sc, w, h, 4 * k);
  y += (dn - 1) / sc;
  on ? (
    col(lens, 1); lk_rr(x, y, w, h - 1 / sc, 4 * k);
    i = 1;
    loop(4, t = 0.07 * i * (1 + 0.6 * max(1 - k, 0));
      dx = (i == 1 ? 3 : i == 2 ? 6 : i == 3 ? 10 : 14) * k;  dy = (i == 1 ? 2 : i == 2 ? 4 : i == 3 ? 7 : 9) * k;
      col(ui_mix(c, 0xFFFFFF, t), 1); lk_rr(x + dx, y + dy, w - 2 * dx, h - 1 / sc - 2 * dy, 4 * k);  i += 1; );
  ) : (
    col(shade(lens, 0.62), 1); lk_rr(x, y, w, h - 1 / sc, 4 * k);
    col(shade(lens, 0.78), 1); lk_rr(x + 2 * k, y + 2 * k, w - 4 * k, h - 5 * k, 4 * k);
    col(shade(lens, 0.92), 1); lk_rr(x + 5 * k, y + 4 * k, w - 10 * k, h - 10 * k, 4 * k);
    col(lens, 1);              lk_rr(x + 9 * k, y + 7 * k, w - 18 * k, h - 17 * k, 4 * k);
  );
  col(0xFFFFFF, on ? 0.45 : 0.22);  gfx_rect(px(x + 4 * k), py(y), ps(w - 8 * k), max(1, ps(1.5)));
  hov && !dn ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.07); lk_rr(x, y, w, h - 1 / sc, 4 * k); );
  gfx_setfont(2);  col(shade(c, on ? 0.30 : 0.17), 1);
  ui_keytext(px(x + w * 0.5), py(y + h * 0.5), str);
  hit;
);
function ck(x, y, w, h, sel, str) local(hov, hit, yy) (
  hov = mouse_x >= px(x) && mouse_x < px(x + w) && mouse_y >= py(y) && mouse_y < py(y + h);
  hit = click && hov && !drag_idx;
  yy = sel ? y : y + 1.5;
  col(0x000000, 0.45);  u_rect(x + 1, yy + 1.5, w, h - 1.5);
  col(sel ? 0xF0E8D2 : 0xB3AE9F, 1);  u_rect(x, yy, w, h - 1.5);
  col(shade(sel ? 0xF0E8D2 : 0xB3AE9F, 0.72), 1);  u_rect(x, yy + h - 3.5, w, 2);  u_rect(x + w - 2, yy, 2, h - 1.5);
  hov ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.1);  u_rect(x, yy, w, h - 1.5); );
  col(0xF2A41E, sel ? 0.35 : 0);  gfx_circle(px(x + w - 9), py(yy + 9), ps(5), 1, 1);
  col(sel ? 0xF2A41E : 0x6A5A40, 1);  gfx_circle(px(x + w - 9), py(yy + 9), ps(2.8), 1, 1);
  gfx_setfont(2);  col(sel ? 0x2A2A28 : 0x4A4840, 1);  text_c(px(x + w * 0.5 - 4), py(yy + h * 0.5), str);
  hit;
);
function lcd_box(x, y, w, h) ( col(0x1C1D1E, 1);  u_rect(x - 2, y - 2, w + 4, h + 4);  col(0x020403, 1);  u_rect(x, y, w, h);  col(C_LCDBG, 1);  u_rect(x + 3, y + 3, w - 6, h - 6); );
function lcd(x, y, w, h, fnt, str) local(tw, th, gy) (
  lcd_box(x, y, w, h);
  gfx_setfont(fnt);  gfx_measurestr(str, tw, th);  gy = py(y + h * 0.5) - th * 0.5;
  col(C_LCDTX, 0.22);  gfx_x = px(x + 10) - 1;  gfx_y = gy;  gfx_drawstr(str);  gfx_x = px(x + 10) + 1;  gfx_y = gy;  gfx_drawstr(str);
  col(C_LCDTX, 1);  gfx_x = px(x + 10);  gfx_y = gy;  gfx_drawstr(str);
);
// a vertical LED meter (-48 .. 0 dB) with its name below
function vmeter(x, y, h, lv, name) local(db, j, d, n) (
  db = lv > 0.000001 ? 8.685889638065035 * log(lv) : -120;  n = 20;
  col(0x0A0B0B, 1);  u_rect(x, y, 22, h);
  j = 0;
  loop(n, d = -48 + (j + 1) * 48 / n;
    col(d > -1 ? 0xFF5A40 : d > -10 ? 0xF2C230 : C_TEAL, db >= d - 2.4 ? 1 : 0.12);
    u_rect(x + 3, y + h - 3 - (j + 1) * (h - 6) / n + 1, 16, (h - 6) / n - 1.5);  j += 1; );
  gfx_setfont(5);  col(C_INK2, 1);  text_c(px(x + 11), py(y + h + 14), name);
);
function pb_count(menu) local(k, n) ( n = 1;  k = 0;  loop(strlen(menu), str_getchar(menu, k) == 124 ? n += 1;  k += 1; );  n; );
function pb_item(menu, i, dst) local(k, k0, n, c, len) (
  strcpy(dst, "");  len = strlen(menu);  k = 0;  k0 = 0;  n = 1;
  loop(len + 1, c = k < len ? str_getchar(menu, k) : 124;  c == 124 ? ( n == i ? strcpy_substr(dst, menu, k0, k - k0);  n += 1;  k0 = k + 1; );  k += 1; );
  dst;
);
function pb_tri(cx, cy, s, dir) ( gfx_triangle(px(cx + dir * s), py(cy), px(cx - dir * s), py(cy - s), px(cx - dir * s), py(cy + s)); );
function preset_bar(x, y, h, lw, cur, menu) local(n, sel, open, lx, i) (
  n = pb_count(menu);  sel = 0;  open = 0;
  lk_key(x, y + 3, 92, h - 6, 0, 0xB8BCBC, "PRESETS") ? open = 1;
  lk_key(x + 102, y + 3, 38, h - 6, 0, 0xB8BCBC, "") ? ( sel = cur <= 1 || cur > n ? n : cur - 1; );
  lk_key(x + 150, y + 3, 38, h - 6, 0, 0xB8BCBC, "") ? ( sel = cur >= n || cur < 1 ? 1 : cur + 1; );
  col(0x1A1B1C, 1);  pb_tri(x + 121, y + h * 0.5, 5, -1);  pb_tri(x + 169, y + h * 0.5, 5, 1);
  lx = x + 202;
  cur >= 1 && cur <= n ? pb_item(menu, cur, #pb_nm) : strcpy(#pb_nm, "--");
  lcd(lx, y, lw, h, 8, #pb_nm);
  click && mouse_x >= px(lx) && mouse_x < px(lx + lw) && mouse_y >= py(y) && mouse_y < py(y + h) ? open = 1;
  open ? (
    strcpy(#pb_m, "");  i = 1;
    loop(n, i == cur ? strcat(#pb_m, "!");  strcat(#pb_m, pb_item(menu, i, #pb_t));  i < n ? strcat(#pb_m, "|");  i += 1; );
    gfx_x = px(x);  gfx_y = py(y + h);  i = gfx_showmenu(#pb_m);  i > 0 ? sel = i;
  );
  sel;
);
// a status LED (lit by lv 0 - 1) in a black ring
function sled(x, y, r, c, lv) ( col(0x050606, 1);  gfx_circle(px(x), py(y), ps(r + 2), 1, 1);  col(ui_mix(shade(c, 0.3), c, min(1, lv)), 1);  gfx_circle(px(x), py(y), ps(r), 1, 1);
  lv > 0.05 ? ( col(c, 0.25 * min(1, lv));  gfx_circle(px(x), py(y), ps(r * 2.2), 1, 1); ); );
// a KEY + LED: a small square key, its own green LED beside it
function kled(x, y, w, h, on, str) local(hov, hit) (
  hov = mouse_x >= px(x) && mouse_x < px(x + w) && mouse_y >= py(y) && mouse_y < py(y + h);  hit = click && hov && !drag_idx;
  col(0x000000, 0.35);  u_rect(x + 1, y + 3, w + 2, h + 2);  col(0x050606, 1);  u_rect(x - 2, y - 2, w + 4, h + 4);
  col(on ? 0xE8E2CC : 0xA8A390, 1);  u_rect(x, y, w, h);  col(0xFFFFFF, 0.3);  u_rect(x, y, w, 2);  col(0x000000, 0.12);  u_rect(x, y + h - 4, w, 4);  u_rect(x + w - 3, y, 3, h);
  hov ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.08);  u_rect(x, y, w, h); );
  gfx_setfont(2);  col(0x1E1E1C, 1);  text_c(px(x + w * 0.5), py(y + h * 0.5), str);
  sled(x + w + 16, y + h * 0.5, 5, 0x7CE05A, on);
  hit;
);
// a dark DISPLAY BOX (a choice from a menu), light text; returns 1 when clicked
function dbox(x, y, w, h, str) local(hov) (
  hov = mouse_x >= px(x) && mouse_x < px(x + w) && mouse_y >= py(y) && mouse_y < py(y + h);
  col(0x000000, 0.45);  u_rect(x - 1, y - 1, w + 2, h + 2);  col(C_LCDBG, 1);  u_rect(x, y, w, h);  col(0xFFFFFF, hov ? 0.12 : 0.06);  u_rect(x, y + h - 1, w, 1);
  gfx_setfont(2);  col(C_LCDTX, 1);  text_c(px(x + w * 0.5), py(y + h * 0.5), str);
  click && hov && !drag_idx;
);

// ---------- the faceplate's own pieces ----------
// brushed gunmetal, painted once into image 121 (again on resize)
function wx_rnd() ( wx_s = (wx_s * 16807) % 2147483647;  wx_s / 2147483647; );
function wx_build() local(i, y, a) (
  gfx_setimgdim(121, ceil(ps(1200)), ceil(ps(902)));  gfx_dest = 121;
  col(C_FACE, 1);  gfx_rect(0, 0, ps(1200), ps(902), 1);
  wx_s = 4431;  i = 0;
  loop(900, y = wx_rnd() * 902;  a = 0.015 + 0.03 * wx_rnd();
    col(wx_rnd() < 0.5 ? 0x000000 : 0xFFFFFF, a);  gfx_line(ps(wx_rnd() * 1200), ps(y), ps(wx_rnd() * 1200 + 60), ps(y), 1);  i += 1; );
  gfx_dest = -1;  wx_sc = sc;
);
// the small square grey key with its red LED set into it (THICK)
function gkey(x, y, s, on, str) local(hov, hit) (
  hov = mouse_x >= px(x) && mouse_x < px(x + s) && mouse_y >= py(y) && mouse_y < py(y + s);  hit = click && hov && !drag_idx;
  shd_r(x - 2, y - 2, s + 4, s + 4);  col(0x0A0C0C, 1);  u_rect(x - 2, y - 2, s + 4, s + 4);
  col(on ? 0xB4B8BC : 0x989CA0, 1);  u_rect(x, y, s, s);  col(0xFFFFFF, 0.3);  u_rect(x, y, s, 2);  u_rect(x, y, 2, s);
  col(0x000000, 0.15);  u_rect(x, y + s - 3, s, 3);  u_rect(x + s - 3, y, 3, s);
  hov ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.08);  u_rect(x, y, s, s); );
  col(0x1A0A08, 1);  gfx_circle(px(x + s * 0.5), py(y + s * 0.5), ps(4.5), 1, 1);
  col(on ? 0xFF3A22 : 0x5A1810, 1);  gfx_circle(px(x + s * 0.5), py(y + s * 0.5), ps(3.2), 1, 1);
  on ? ( col(0xFF3A22, 0.3);  gfx_circle(px(x + s * 0.5), py(y + s * 0.5), ps(7), 1, 1); );
  gfx_setfont(5);  col(C_INK, 1);  text_l(px(x + s + 10), py(y + s * 0.5), str);
  hit;
);
// the CZ key (from the reference photos): a flat rectangular cap - BLUE (modes), GREY (parameters), BLACK (functions),
// RED - with a slight bevel, the legend printed on it, and its own small red LED (led: 1 above the key, 2 set into its
// left end, 0 none)
function cz_key(x, y, w, h, on, kind, led, str) local(hov, hit, dn, c, ink, lx, ly, lc) (
  lc = cz_lc ? cz_lc : 0xFF3828;  cz_lc = 0;                            // (an IN key's LED is amber)
  hov = mouse_x >= px(x) && mouse_x < px(x + w) && mouse_y >= py(y) && mouse_y < py(y + h);  hit = click && hov && !drag_idx;
  dn = hov && lmb ? 1 : 0;
  c = cz_cap ? cz_cap : kind == 0 ? 0x6E9CDC : kind == 1 ? 0x8C9298 : kind == 2 ? 0x24262A : 0xD8483A;  cz_cap = 0;   // (cz_cap: a colour of its own)
  ink = kind == 2 ? 0xE8EAEC : kind == 3 ? 0xFFF4F0 : 0x14171C;
  shd_r(x, y, w, h);
  col(0x050607, 1);  u_rect(x - 1, y - 1, w + 2, h + 2);
  y += dn;
  col(c, 1);  u_rect(x, y, w, h);
  col(0xFFFFFF, kind == 2 ? 0.16 : 0.32);  u_rect(x, y, w, 1.5);  u_rect(x, y, 1.5, h);       // light from the top left
  col(0x000000, 0.22);  u_rect(x, y + h - 2.5, w, 2.5);  u_rect(x + w - 2, y, 2, h);
  col(0x000000, 0.06);  u_rect(x + 2, y + 2, w - 4, h - 4);                                   // a faint vignette
  hov && !dn ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.07);  u_rect(x, y, w, h); );
  led == 1 ? ( lx = x + w * 0.5 - 6;  ly = y - 10 - dn; ) : led == 2 ? ( lx = x + 7;  ly = y + h * 0.5 - 2.5; ) : 0;
  led ? (
    col(0x0A0405, 1);  u_rect(lx - 1, ly - 1, 14, 7);
    col(on ? lc : shade(lc, 0.28), 1);  u_rect(lx, ly, 12, 5);
    on ? ( col(lc, 0.25);  u_rect(lx - 3, ly - 3, 18, 11);  col(0xFFFFFF, 0.45);  u_rect(lx + 1, ly + 1, 5, 1.2); );
  );
  gfx_setfont(2);  col(ink, 1);  text_c(px(x + w * 0.5 + (led == 2 ? 8 : 0)), py(y + h * 0.5), str);
  hit;
);
function tlamp(x, y, c, on) (
  col(0x0A0B0B, 1);  gfx_circle(px(x), py(y), ps(10), 1, 1);
  col(0xEDE6D2, 1);  gfx_circle(px(x), py(y), ps(8), 1, 1);
  col(on ? c : shade(c, 0.35), 1);  gfx_circle(px(x), py(y), ps(5.5), 1, 1);
  on ? ( col(c, 0.25);  gfx_circle(px(x), py(y), ps(14), 1, 1); );
  click && !drag_idx && sqr(mouse_x - px(x)) + sqr(mouse_y - py(y)) < sqr(ps(13));
);
// a light readout box with dark figures (a value read at a glance)
function rbox(x, y, w, h, str) ( col(0x2A2D30, 1);  u_rect(x - 1, y - 1, w + 2, h + 2);  col(0xE6E4DA, 1);  u_rect(x, y, w, h);
  col(0x000000, 0.12);  u_rect(x, y, w, 2);  u_rect(x, y, 2, h);  gfx_setfont(2);  col(0x1C1C1A, 1);  text_c(px(x + w * 0.5), py(y + h * 0.5), str); );
function wcol(w) ( w == 0 ? 0xF2B5C4 : w == 1 ? 0xF6C9A2 : w == 2 ? 0xF1E2A0 : w == 3 ? 0xBFE3C3 : w == 4 ? 0xA9DCD9 : w == 5 ? 0xAFC6EE : w == 6 ? 0xC9B9EC : 0xE6B8DD; );   // the waves' pastels
function wname(w) ( w == 0 ? "SAW" : w == 1 ? "SQUARE" : w == 2 ? "PULSE" : w == 3 ? "DOUBLE" : w == 4 ? "SAW-PULSE" : w == 5 ? "RESO I" : w == 6 ? "RESO II" : "RESO III"; );

// ---------- the ENVELOPE editor: 8 steps (rate, level), drawn; drag a point (up / down = level, left / right = rate) ----------
function seg_w(r) ( 10 + 70 * log(rtime(r) / 0.0015) / log(2) / 11.4; );
function env_edit(x, y, w, h) local(eb, i, tx, xs, sc_, x0, y0, yb, hh, lx, ly, px_, py_, su, en, d, best, bd, mx, my, a, lv, cur, cv, fr, xp, yp, hold)
(
  eb = E + (ui_line * 3 + ui_env) * ES;  su = eb[16];  en = eb[17];
  lcd_box(x, y, w, h);
  x0 = x + 16;  yb = y + h - 14;  hh = h - 48;  y0 = yb - hh;  hold = 34;
  // the x of each step's point (scaled to fit)
  tx = 0;  i = 0;  loop(8, tx += seg_w(eb[i]) + (i == su ? hold : 0);  i += 1; );
  sc_ = min(1, (w - 40) / tx);
  xs = x0;  i = 0;  loop(8, xs += seg_w(eb[i]) * sc_;  EPX[i] = xs;  EPY[i] = yb - eb[8 + i] / 99 * hh;  i == su ? xs += hold * sc_;  i += 1; );
  // grid
  col(C_LCDTX, 0.08);  i = 0;  loop(5, u_rect(x0, y0 + hh * i / 4, w - 32, 1);  i += 1; );
  // the curve: steps after END dim
  lx = x0;  ly = yb;  i = 0;
  loop(8,
    col(C_LCDTX, i <= en ? 0.95 : 0.25);
    gfx_line(px(lx), py(ly), px(EPX[i]), py(EPY[i]), 1);  gfx_line(px(lx), py(ly) + 1, px(EPX[i]), py(EPY[i]) + 1, 1);
    lx = EPX[i];  ly = EPY[i];
    i == su ? ( col(C_LCDTX, 0.5);  xp = lx;  loop(floor(hold * sc_ / 6), u_rect(xp, ly, 3, 1.5);  xp += 6; );  lx += hold * sc_; );
    i += 1;
  );
  // the points: SUSTAIN ringed, END boxed, the chosen step bigger
  i = 0;
  loop(8,
    col(C_LCDTX, i <= en ? 1 : 0.35);  gfx_circle(px(EPX[i]), py(EPY[i]), ps(i == ui_step ? 6 : 4), 1, 1);
    i == ui_step ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.9);  gfx_circle(px(EPX[i]), py(EPY[i]), ps(8), 0, 1); );
    i == su ? ( col(C_LCDTX, 1);  gfx_setfont(5);  text_c(px(EPX[i]), py(EPY[i] - 16), "S"); );
    i == en ? ( col(C_LCDTX, 1);  gfx_setfont(5);  text_c(px(EPX[i]), py(min(EPY[i] + 16, yb + 6)), "E"); );
    i += 1;
  );
  // where the newest voice is now
  ev_on_d ? (
    cur = EV[(ui_line * 3 + ui_env) * 2 + 1];  cv = EV[(ui_line * 3 + ui_env) * 2];
    lv = cur == 0 ? 0 : eb[8 + cur - 1] / 99;  a = eb[8 + cur] / 99;
    fr = abs(a - lv) > 0.001 ? max(0, min(1, (cv - lv) / (a - lv))) : 1;
    xp = (cur == 0 ? x0 : EPX[cur - 1] + (cur - 1 == su ? hold * sc_ : 0)) + fr * (EPX[cur] - (cur == 0 ? x0 : EPX[cur - 1] + (cur - 1 == su ? hold * sc_ : 0)));
    yp = yb - cv * hh;
    col(0xFFF4C0, 0.35);  gfx_circle(px(xp), py(yp), ps(9), 1, 1);  col(0xFFF4C0, 1);  gfx_circle(px(xp), py(yp), ps(4), 1, 1);
  );
  // the text line (apart from the picture)
  gfx_setfont(7);  col(C_LCDTX, 0.9);
  text_l(px(x + 14), py(y + 15), sprintf(#et, "LINE %d  %s   STEP %d   RATE %d   LEVEL %d", ui_line + 1, ui_env == 0 ? "DCO" : ui_env == 1 ? "DCW" : "DCA", ui_step + 1, eb[ui_step], eb[8 + ui_step]));
  // mouse: pick the nearest point, drag it
  mx = (mouse_x - ox) / sc;  my = (mouse_y - oy) / (sc * YS);
  click && !drag_idx && mx >= x && mx < x + w && my >= y + 26 && my < y + h ? (
    best = -1;  bd = 18 * 18;  i = 0;
    loop(8, d = sqr(mx - EPX[i]) + sqr(my - EPY[i]);  d < bd ? ( bd = d;  best = i; );  i += 1; );
    best >= 0 ? ( ui_step = best;  e_drag = 1;  e_mx = mx;  e_my = my;  e_r0 = eb[best];  e_l0 = eb[8 + best]; );
  );
  e_drag && lmb ? (
    d = (mouse_cap & 8) ? 0.25 : 1;
    eb[8 + ui_step] = max(0, min(99, floor(e_l0 + (e_my - my) / hh * 99 * d + 0.5)));
    eb[ui_step] = max(0, min(99, floor(e_r0 - (mx - e_mx) / 3 * d + 0.5)));        // to the right = slower
  );
  !lmb ? e_drag = 0;
  mx >= x && mx < x + w && my >= y && my < y + h && mouse_wheel != 0 ? (
    (mouse_cap & 8) ? eb[ui_step] = max(0, min(99, eb[ui_step] + sign(mouse_wheel))) : eb[8 + ui_step] = max(0, min(99, eb[8 + ui_step] + sign(mouse_wheel)));
    mouse_wheel = 0; );
);

// ---------- presets (checkpoint 3 brings the set) ----------
PRESET_MENU = "Default|Glass Bell|Phase Strings|Electric Piano|Brass Lead|Resonant Sweep|Ambient Pad|Metallic Pluck|Dirty Sync Bass|Chorus Organ|Sci-Fi FX|Soft Evolution|Synth Bass|Breathy Flute|Funky Clav|Vibes|Reso Lead|Sync Lead|Digital Choir|Tubular Bells|Marimba|Harpsichord|Reso Bass|Night Wind|Space Choir|Synth Strings|Space Flute";
EPX = 1040;  EPY = 1050;

// ---------- frame ----------
g_ret = gfx_ext_retina > 1 ? gfx_ext_retina : 1;
g_want = ui_sz == 1 ? 0.85 : ui_sz == 2 ? 1.3 : 1;
sc = g_ret * max(min(g_want, min(gfx_w / (1200 * g_ret), gfx_h / (902 * g_ret))), 0.5);
ox = (gfx_w - 1200 * sc) * 0.5;  oy = (gfx_h - 902 * sc) * 0.5;
lmb = mouse_cap & 1;  click = lmb && !last_lmb;  klog = 0;  kstep = 0;
gfx_setfont(1, "Trebuchet MS", ps(34), 'b');
gfx_setfont(2, "Trebuchet MS", ps(14), 'b');
gfx_setfont(3, "Trebuchet MS", ps(14), 'b');
gfx_setfont(4, "Trebuchet MS", ps(17), 'b');
gfx_setfont(5, "Trebuchet MS", ps(12.5), 'b');
gfx_setfont(6, "Trebuchet MS", ps(14.5), 'b');
gfx_setfont(7, "Courier New", ps(15), 'b');
gfx_setfont(8, "Courier New", ps(19), 'b');
gfx_setfont(10, "Trebuchet MS", ps(13), 'b');
out_m = max(outpk_disp, out_m * 0.85);  outpk_disp = 0;

// ---------- faceplate ----------
col(0x101112, 1);  gfx_rect(0, 0, gfx_w, gfx_h, 1);
wx_sc != sc ? wx_build();
gfx_a = 1;  gfx_x = px(0);  gfx_y = py(0);  gfx_blit(121, 1, 0);
col(0x000000, 0.4);  u_rect(0, 816, 1200, 4);  u_rect(1196, 0, 4, 820);
rivet(12, 12);  rivet(1188, 12);  rivet(12, 808);  rivet(1188, 808);
gfx_setfont(1);  col(C_INK, 1);  text_l(px(36), py(36), "CZ77"); ver_tag("v2", 16, 5.05, 0);
// the amber pilot lamp (lit while IN)
col(0x0A0A0A, 1);  gfx_circle(px(146), py(36), ps(9), 1, 1);
col(in_on >= 0.5 ? 0xFFB238 : 0x5A3A10, 1);  gfx_circle(px(146), py(36), ps(6.5), 1, 1);
in_on >= 0.5 ? ( col(0xFFB238, 0.22);  gfx_circle(px(146), py(36), ps(14), 1, 1);  col(0xFFFFFF, 0.6);  gfx_circle(px(144), py(34), ps(2), 1, 1); );
gfx_setfont(10);  col(C_INK2, 1);  text_l(px(170), py(28), "PHASE DISTORTION");  text_l(px(170), py(46), "SYNTHESISER");
prs_cur_d > 0 ? ( pr_cur = prs_cur_d; prs_cur_d = 0; );     // PRESET parameter: show a preset loaded by the host
pb_k = preset_bar(440, 18, 34, 340, pr_cur, PRESET_MENU);
pb_k > 0 ? ( prs_dirty = pb_k;  pr_cur = pb_k; );
// voice lamps on a light inset
col(0xC9CCCF, 1);  u_rect(996, 23, 104, 26);  col(0x000000, 0.25);  u_rect(996, 23, 104, 2);  u_rect(996, 23, 2, 26);
g_j = 0;
loop(8, g_v = VD[g_j];  col(0x1A1B1C, 1);  gfx_circle(px(1008 + g_j * 12), py(36), ps(4.6), 1, 1);
  col(0xFF6A30, 0.15 + 0.85 * min(1, g_v * 2));  gfx_circle(px(1008 + g_j * 12), py(36), ps(3.4), 1, 1);  g_j += 1; );
col(C_RULE, 0.8);  u_rect(16, 66, 1168, 2);

// ---------- LINES ----------
section(16, 80, 336, 254, C_SEC1, "LINES");
g_j = 0;
loop(4,
  cz_key(32 + (g_j % 2) * 158, 134 + floor(g_j / 2) * 48, 146, 32, floor(line_md + 0.5) == g_j, 0, 1,
    g_j == 0 ? "LINE 1" : g_j == 1 ? "LINE 2" : g_j == 2 ? "1 + 2" : "1 + 1'") ? ( slider(1) = g_j;  param_touched(1); );
  g_j += 1;
);
cz_key(32, 234, 94, 24, ring >= 0.5, 2, 2, "RING") ? ( slider(2) = ring >= 0.5 ? 0 : 1;  param_touched(2); );
cz_key(134, 234, 94, 24, noise >= 0.5, 2, 2, "NOISE") ? ( slider(3) = noise >= 0.5 ? 0 : 1;  param_touched(3); );
cz_key(242, 234, 94, 24, mono >= 0.5, 2, 2, "MONO") ? ( slider(54) = mono >= 0.5 ? 0 : 1;  param_touched(54); );
gfx_setfont(5);  col(C_INK2, 1);  text_c(px(64), py(270), "OCTAVE");  text_c(px(142), py(270), "NOTE");
dbox(32, 282, 64, 28, det_oct == 0 ? "0" : sprintf(#do, "%+d", det_oct)) ? (
  gfx_x = px(32);  gfx_y = py(312);  g_i = gfx_showmenu(sprintf(#dm, "%s+2|%s+1|%s0|%s-1|%s-2", det_oct == 2 ? "!" : "", det_oct == 1 ? "!" : "", det_oct == 0 ? "!" : "", det_oct == -1 ? "!" : "", det_oct == -2 ? "!" : ""));
  g_i > 0 ? ( slider(8) = 3 - g_i;  param_touched(8); ); );
dbox(110, 282, 64, 28, sprintf(#dn, "+%d", det_note)) ? (
  gfx_x = px(110);  gfx_y = py(312);  strcpy(#nm, "");  g_i = 0;
  loop(12, g_i == det_note ? strcat(#nm, "!");  strcat(#nm, sprintf(#ns, "+%d", g_i));  g_i < 11 ? strcat(#nm, "|");  g_i += 1; );
  g_i = gfx_showmenu(#nm);  g_i > 0 ? ( slider(9) = g_i - 1;  param_touched(9); ); );
kn(216, 290, 17, 10, 0, 60, 0, "FINE", 5);
klog = 1;  kn(296, 290, 17, 55, 1, 2000, 80, "GLIDE", 15);
(line_md < 1.5) ? ( col(C_SEC1, 0.55);  u_rect(24, 262, 230, 68); );       // DETUNE: for 1 + 2 and 1 + 1'
line_md < 1.5 ? ( col(C_SEC1, 0.55);  u_rect(24, 226, 210, 36); );         // RING and NOISE: with both lines (NOISE with line 2)
mono < 0.5 ? ( col(C_SEC1, 0.55);  u_rect(256, 262, 88, 68); );            // GLIDE: in MONO

// ---------- WAVES ----------
section(364, 80, 820, 254, C_SEC2, "WAVES");
g_j = 0;
loop(2, cz_key(976 + g_j * 100, 86, 92, 24, ui_line == g_j, 1, 2, g_j == 0 ? "LINE 1" : "LINE 2") ? ui_line = g_j;  g_j += 1; );
gfx_setfont(5);  col(C_INK2, 1);  text_l(px(380), py(124), "WAVE");  text_l(px(380), py(190), "SECOND WAVE (alternates with the first)");
g_w1 = floor(slider(ui_line ? 6 : 4) + 0.5);  g_w2 = floor(slider(ui_line ? 7 : 5) + 0.5) - 1;
g_j = 0;
loop(8,
  cz_cap = wcol(g_j);  cz_key(380 + g_j * 100, 144, 92, 30, g_w1 == g_j, 1, 1, wname(g_j)) ? ( slider(ui_line ? 6 : 4) = g_j;  param_touched(ui_line ? 6 : 4); );
  cz_cap = wcol(g_j);  cz_key(380 + g_j * 100, 210, 92, 30, g_w2 == g_j, 1, 1, wname(g_j)) ? ( slider(ui_line ? 7 : 5) = g_w2 == g_j ? 0 : g_j + 1;  param_touched(ui_line ? 7 : 5); );
  g_j += 1;
);
kn(440, 284, 18, 15, 0, 100, 100, "DCW DEPTH", 1);
kn(580, 284, 18, ui_line ? 13 : 11, 0, 100, 30, "DCW FOLLOW", 1);
kn(720, 284, 18, ui_line ? 14 : 12, 0, 100, 30, "DCA FOLLOW", 1);
kn(860, 284, 18, 16, -24, 6, 0, "LINE 2 LEVEL", 4);
kn(1000, 284, 18, 22, 0, 100, 50, "VELOCITY", 1);
line_md >= 2.5 && ui_line == 1 ? ( col(C_SEC2, 0.6);  u_rect(372, 116, 804, 124);  gfx_setfont(6);  col(C_INK, 1);  text_c(px(774), py(176), "1 + 1': LINE 2 PLAYS LINE 1, DETUNED"); );

// ---------- FILTER ----------
section(772, 346, 200, 266, C_SEC3, "FILTER");
g_m = floor(flt_md + 0.5);
dbox(792, 390, 160, 30, g_m == 0 ? "OFF" : g_m == 1 ? "LOW-PASS" : g_m == 2 ? "BAND-PASS" : "HIGH-PASS") ? (
  gfx_x = px(792);  gfx_y = py(422);
  g_i = gfx_showmenu(sprintf(#fm, "%sOff|%sLow-pass|%sBand-pass|%sHigh-pass", g_m == 0 ? "!" : "", g_m == 1 ? "!" : "", g_m == 2 ? "!" : "", g_m == 3 ? "!" : ""));
  g_i > 0 ? ( slider(17) = g_i - 1;  param_touched(17); ); );
klog = 1;  kn(822, 476, 18, 18, 40, 20000, 8000, "CUTOFF", 9);
kn(922, 476, 18, 19, 0, 100, 0, "RESO", 1);
kn(822, 560, 18, 20, 0, 100, 0, "KEY TRACK", 1);
kn(922, 560, 18, 21, -100, 100, 0, "ENV", 1);
g_m == 0 ? ( col(C_SEC3, 0.55);  u_rect(780, 432, 184, 176); );

// ---------- ENVELOPES ----------
section(16, 346, 744, 266, C_SEC2, "ENVELOPES");
g_j = 0;
loop(3, cz_key(32 + g_j * 128, 392, 112, 30, ui_env == g_j, 1, 2, g_j == 0 ? "DCO" : g_j == 1 ? "DCW" : "DCA") ? ui_env = g_j;  g_j += 1; );
env_edit(32, 438, 512, 160);
// the chosen step: its number (arrows), RATE and LEVEL; the SUSTAIN and END steps
g_eb = E + (ui_line * 3 + ui_env) * ES;
gfx_setfont(5);  col(C_INK2, 1);  text_c(px(658), py(422), "STEP");
cz_key(564, 434, 30, 28, 0, 2, 0, "") ? ui_step = max(0, ui_step - 1);
cz_key(722, 434, 30, 28, 0, 2, 0, "") ? ui_step = min(7, ui_step + 1);
col(0xE8EAEC, 1);  pb_tri(579, 448, 5, -1);  pb_tri(737, 448, 5, 1);
rbox(604, 434, 108, 28, sprintf(#sn, "%d", ui_step + 1));
gfx_setfont(5);  col(C_INK2, 1);  text_c(px(608), py(484), "RATE");  text_c(px(708), py(484), "LEVEL");
rbox(568, 496, 80, 28, sprintf(#rv, "%d", g_eb[ui_step]));  rbox(668, 496, 80, 28, sprintf(#lv, "%d", g_eb[8 + ui_step]));
gfx_setfont(5);  col(C_INK2, 1);  text_c(px(608), py(546), "SUSTAIN");  text_c(px(708), py(546), "END");
g_su = g_eb[16];  g_en = g_eb[17];
dbox(568, 558, 80, 28, g_su < 0 ? "OFF" : sprintf(#su, "STEP %d", g_su + 1)) ? (
  gfx_x = px(568);  gfx_y = py(588);  strcpy(#sm, g_su < 0 ? "!Off|" : "Off|");  g_i = 0;
  loop(8, g_i == g_su ? strcat(#sm, "!");  strcat(#sm, sprintf(#ss, "Step %d", g_i + 1));  g_i < 7 ? strcat(#sm, "|");  g_i += 1; );
  g_i = gfx_showmenu(#sm);  g_i > 0 ? ( g_eb[16] = g_i - 2;  g_eb[16] > g_eb[17] ? g_eb[17] = g_eb[16]; ); );
dbox(668, 558, 80, 28, sprintf(#en, "STEP %d", g_en + 1)) ? (
  gfx_x = px(668);  gfx_y = py(588);  strcpy(#em, "");  g_i = 0;
  loop(8, g_i == g_en ? strcat(#em, "!");  strcat(#em, sprintf(#ens, "Step %d", g_i + 1));  g_i < 7 ? strcat(#em, "|");  g_i += 1; );
  g_i = gfx_showmenu(#em);  g_i > 0 ? ( g_eb[17] = g_i - 1;  g_eb[16] > g_eb[17] ? g_eb[16] = g_eb[17]; ); );

// ---------- VIBRATO ----------
section(984, 346, 200, 266, C_SEC1, "VIBRATO");
g_m = floor(vib_wv + 0.5);
dbox(1004, 390, 160, 30, g_m == 0 ? "TRIANGLE" : g_m == 1 ? "SAW UP" : g_m == 2 ? "SAW DOWN" : "SQUARE") ? (
  gfx_x = px(1004);  gfx_y = py(422);
  g_i = gfx_showmenu(sprintf(#vm, "%sTriangle|%sSaw up|%sSaw down|%sSquare", g_m == 0 ? "!" : "", g_m == 1 ? "!" : "", g_m == 2 ? "!" : "", g_m == 3 ? "!" : ""));
  g_i > 0 ? ( slider(23) = g_i - 1;  param_touched(23); ); );
kn(1034, 476, 18, 24, 0, 3, 0.3, "DELAY", 8);
klog = 1;  kn(1134, 476, 18, 25, 0.1, 12, 5, "RATE", 7);
kn(1034, 560, 18, 26, 0, 100, 0, "DEPTH", 5);
kn(1134, 560, 18, 56, 0, 100, 0, "DCW MOD", 1);

// ---------- the FX strip: PHASER, CHORUS, DRIVE, COMP, DELAY (each with its title lamp) ----------
function fx_sec(x, c, title, idx) local(on) (
  section(x, 624, 177, 180, c, "");
  on = slider(idx) >= 0.5;
  tlamp(x + 22, 644, 0xFFB238, on) ? ( slider(idx) = on ? 0 : 1;  param_touched(idx); );
  gfx_setfont(4);  col(C_INK, 1);  text_l(px(x + 40), py(643), title);
  on;
);
g_on = fx_sec(16, C_SEC3, "PHASER", 31);
klog = 1;  kn(66, 690, 16, 32, 0.05, 8, 0.4, "RATE", 7);
kn(144, 690, 16, 33, 0, 100, 60, "DEPTH", 1);
kn(66, 758, 16, 34, 0, 90, 40, "FEEDBACK", 1);
!g_on ? ( col(C_SEC3, 0.5);  u_rect(22, 662, 165, 138); );
g_on = fx_sec(205, C_SEC1, "CHORUS", 35);
klog = 1;  kn(255, 690, 16, 36, 0.25, 4, 1, "RATE", 13);
kn(333, 690, 16, 37, 0, 100, 60, "DEPTH", 1);
kn(255, 758, 16, 38, 0, 100, 50, "MIX", 1);
!g_on ? ( col(C_SEC1, 0.5);  u_rect(211, 662, 165, 138); );
g_on = fx_sec(394, C_SEC3, "DRIVE", 39);
kn(444, 690, 16, 40, 0, 100, 30, "AMOUNT", 1);
kn(522, 690, 16, 41, 0, 100, 60, "TONE", 1);
!g_on ? ( col(C_SEC3, 0.5);  u_rect(400, 662, 165, 138); );
g_on = fx_sec(583, C_SEC1, "COMP", 42);
kn(633, 690, 16, 43, -40, 0, -18, "THRESHOLD", 4);
klog = 1;  kn(711, 690, 16, 44, 1, 20, 4, "RATIO", 14);
klog = 1;  kn(633, 758, 16, 45, 0.1, 100, 10, "ATTACK", 15);
klog = 1;  kn(711, 758, 16, 46, 10, 1000, 150, "RELEASE", 15);
// gain reduction: a short LED row in the title band
gr_m = max(gr_disp, gr_m * 0.85);  gr_disp = 0;
g_j = 0;  loop(6, col(0x0A0B0B, 1);  u_rect(686 + g_j * 11, 638, 9, 10);  col(0xFF3828, gr_m >= (g_j + 1) * 2 - 1 ? 1 : 0.15);  u_rect(687 + g_j * 11, 639, 7, 8);  g_j += 1; );
!g_on ? ( col(C_SEC1, 0.5);  u_rect(589, 662, 165, 138); );
g_on = fx_sec(772, C_SEC3, "DELAY", 47);
cz_key(874, 631, 62, 22, 0, dl_sync >= 0.5 ? 0 : 1, 0, "SYNC") ? ( slider(48) = dl_sync >= 0.5 ? 0 : 1;  param_touched(48); );
dl_sync >= 0.5 ? ( kstep = 1;  kn(822, 690, 16, 49, 0, 12, 7, "TIME", 16); ) : ( klog = 1;  kn(822, 690, 16, 50, 10, 2000, 375, "TIME", 8); );
kn(900, 690, 16, 51, 0, 95, 35, "FEEDBACK", 1);
klog = 1;  kn(822, 758, 16, 52, 1000, 18000, 5000, "DAMPING", 9);
kn(900, 758, 16, 53, 0, 100, 25, "MIX", 1);
!g_on ? ( col(C_SEC3, 0.5);  u_rect(778, 662, 165, 138); );

// ---------- OUTPUT ----------
section(964, 624, 220, 180, C_SEC2, "OUTPUT");
cz_lc = 0xFFA820;  cz_key(1112, 630, 60, 24, in_on >= 0.5, 2, 2, "IN") ? ( slider(29) = in_on >= 0.5 ? 0 : 1;  param_touched(29); );
kn(1010, 706, 22, 27, -18, 6, 0, "LEVEL", 4);
kn(1088, 706, 15, 28, 0, 100, 50, "DRIFT", 1);
gkey(992, 764, 22, thick >= 0.5, "THICK") ? ( slider(30) = thick >= 0.5 ? 0 : 1;  param_touched(30); );
vmeter(1146, 664, 112, out_m, "OUT");

// ---------- S / M / L / ? ----------
g_j = 0;
loop(4,
  g_x = 1118 + g_j * 14;  g_on = g_j == 0 ? ui_sz == 1 : g_j == 1 ? ui_sz == 0 : g_j == 2 ? ui_sz == 2 : sz_help;
  col(0x0A0B0B, 1);  u_rect(g_x, 27, 13, 18);
  col(g_on ? 0xFFB238 : 0x6A6E72, 1);  u_rect(g_x + 1, 28, 11, 16);
  gfx_setfont(5);  col(g_on ? 0x1A1206 : C_INK, 1);  text_c(px(g_x + 6.5), py(36), g_j == 0 ? "S" : g_j == 1 ? "M" : g_j == 2 ? "L" : "?");
  click && !sz_help && mouse_x >= px(g_x) && mouse_x < px(g_x + 13) && mouse_y >= py(27) && mouse_y < py(45) ? (
    g_j == 0 ? ui_sz = 1 : g_j == 1 ? ui_sz = 0 : g_j == 2 ? ui_sz = 2 : ( sz_help = 1;  sz_new = 1; );
  );
  g_j += 1;
);
sz_help && click && !sz_new ? sz_help = 0;
sz_new = 0;
sz_help ? (
  col(0x000000, 0.62);  gfx_rect(0, 0, gfx_w, gfx_h, 1);
  strcpy(#hl3, "Manual - https://www.gardenfx.uk/manual/");  strcat(#hl3, #ui_man);  strcat(#hl3, ".pdf");
  gfx_setfont(5);  gfx_measurestr(#hl3, g_tw, g_th);
  g_cw = max(g_tw + ps(40), ps(380));  g_ch = ps(130);  g_cx = (gfx_w - g_cw) * 0.5;  g_cy = (gfx_h - g_ch) * 0.5;
  col(0x000000, 0.5);  ui_rrs(g_cx + ps(3), g_cy + ps(5), g_cw, g_ch, ps(8));
  col(0x1C1D20, 1);    ui_rrs(g_cx, g_cy, g_cw, g_ch, ps(8));
  col(0xE0603A, 1);    gfx_rect(g_cx + ps(20), g_cy + ps(36), g_cw - ps(40), max(1, ps(1)), 1);
  gfx_setfont(6);  col(0xF2F2EE, 1);  gfx_x = g_cx + ps(20);  gfx_y = g_cy + ps(14);  gfx_drawstr("Design by JGWizrad.  © John Garden 2026");
  gfx_setfont(5);  col(0xE8B23A, 1);  gfx_x = g_cx + ps(20);  gfx_y = g_cy + ps(50);  gfx_drawstr("https://www.gardenfx.uk/");
  col(0xD8D6D0, 1);  gfx_x = g_cx + ps(20);  gfx_y = g_cy + ps(72);  gfx_drawstr(#hl3);
  col(0x85837E, 1);  gfx_x = g_cx + ps(20);  gfx_y = g_cy + ps(102);  gfx_drawstr("Click anywhere to close.");
);
!lmb ? drag_idx = 0;
mouse_wheel = 0;
last_lmb = lmb;
gui_dirty ? ( prm_dirty = 1;  gui_dirty = 0; );
